&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Business Value Consulting team focuses on driving long-term growth and value creation for the largest and most strategic Stripe users. Business Value Consultants play a critical role in translating the technical capabilities of Stripe products into strategic value for customers. We help drive meaningful business outcomes and accelerate decision-making through a consultative approach that aims to build investment confidence and improve CxO conversations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Business Value Consulting team partners closely with our Go-to-market teams and Enterprise users to articulate the strategic value Stripe will provide for users’ businesses. Value Consultants develop methodologies to measure the financial, strategic, and operational benefits Stripe provides, and use those to develop value propositions, business cases, and ROI justifications for our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build compelling business case presentations and ROI (Return on Investment) analyses aimed at accelerating, justifying, or expanding sales opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create ROI tools for sales and customers for joint business casing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Craft high-impact, executive-level narrative and presentations for CxOs while working cross-functionally with our Sales and Presales teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct internal and external research around customers’ businesses, market, industry, and functional trends, and business value analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong relationships with regional sales leaders to be a key driver on strategic account planning and engagements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create assets for internal teams to articulate and measure the value of Stripe and deliver high-level business value impact in a consistent way&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the creation and management of library assets including value frameworks, and other sales and value capture assets to help scale the team&#39;s reach across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide thought leadership, training, and consultative partnering with internal sales and other teams throughout and beyond the sales cycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in management consulting, business value consulting, strategic finance, or similar roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong financial acumen and demonstrated expertise in building compelling executive-ready ROI models, business cases, and financial frameworks (value metrics, cost-benefit analysis, TCO/TVO) that directly influence buying decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive presence and storytelling ability to translate complex financial narratives into clear, persuasive presentations that resonate with C-suite buyers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to partner with Sales, Solutions Architecture, Product, and Customer Success to shape deal strategy and accelerate revenue outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter who is comfortable managing multiple concurrent engagements with rigor, balancing speed and analytical precision independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the technology, SaaS, or fintech industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in payments, financial services, or digital commerce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA or advanced degree in Business, Finance, Economics, or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of developing scalable frameworks and methodologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of value selling methodologies and sales processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Marketing Strategy &amp;amp; Operations team is responsible for driving organizational effectiveness and leading transformational programs across Marketing, Self-serve, Startup and Sales Development. We create the processes and conditions that enable high performance across teams and help Stripe scale with focus and discipline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We partner closely with the CMO, Marketing and Sales Development leadership team to define strategy, lead operational planning, and steward execution across global programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our work spans cross-functional efforts that are critical to Stripe’s growth. From delivering strategic insights and frameworks to leading complex initiatives, we focus on what moves the needle most for the business. We care about results, not activity, and we have fun doing it. If you like hard problems, are analytical, and are an amazing teammate, we want to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Campaign Strategy &amp;amp; Operations Manager, you&#39;ll own the operational foundation that powers Stripe&#39;s global demand engine — building the systems, processes, and workflows that enable our marketing teams to move faster and perform better at scale. You&#39;ll partner with the Global Campaigns, Demand, and Field Marketing teams to drive strategic planning, design operational processes such as budget management and resource planning, and collaborate across global, regional, and channel teams to execute the end-to-end campaign lifecycle.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-visibility, high-impact role at the intersection of marketing strategy and operational execution — one where the work you build today shapes how the entire demand function operates for years to come.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Global Campaigns, Demand and Field Marketing leadership team on operating cadences and processes, including monthly and quarterly business reviews, annual planning, budget and resource allocation, org-wide goal setting, and communications.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with global, regional, and channel teams to architect and implement scalable operating models to support the end-to-end campaign &amp;amp; event lifecycle, from initial strategy and planning through execution, measurement, and optimization, ensuring seamless integration across various functions and geographies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistently monitor and analyze the campaign production &amp;amp; activation &quot;supply chain&quot; including tracking all key stages, handoffs, and friction points to drive meaningful efficiency gains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently scope and lead strategic programs to solve high-impact problems. This includes developing frameworks, aligning stakeholders, and ensuring execution drives measurable outcomes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track, analyze, and report out on key operational metrics and team performance, clearly communicating the health of the campaign &amp;amp; event supply chain, the impact of operational improvements, and the overall effectiveness of campaigns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage campaign and event analytics to do ad-hoc, deep-dives on user engagement patterns, conversion trends, and growth opportunities across the demand funnel. Use these insights to shape hypotheses, drive prioritization conversations, and identify areas to probe more deeply in partnership with Marketing, Finance and GTM teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring clarity to ambiguity. You’ll navigate complexity, distill insight from noise, resolve issues quickly, and empower teams to make smart, confident decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of demand generation, campaign &amp;amp; marketing operations, strategy and operations, business operations, or similar roles with exposure to both business and technical skills&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven expertise in partnering with regional teams and channel partners to build scalable, end-to-end demand generation workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to deploy AI-powered solutions within campaigns or demand generation with specific, measurable outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in highly cross-functional settings, and in a role that spans strategy, analysis, and operations in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent presentation, writing, and communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Appetite and ability to work through ambiguity with minimal guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong change management background and ability to influence diverse stakeholder groups across global, regional, and technical teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of marketing and how its varied disciplines work together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with project management tools such as Asana, Monday.com, or Jira&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Marketing automation systems and tools&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, finance, fintech, or high-growth technology companies&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in management consulting or program management roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At its core, Stripe is a treasury company, and the Treasury Finance team (TFIN) is key to building the Global Payments and Treasury Network (GPTN).&amp;nbsp; Within TFIN, the FX team collaborates closely with product, engineering, sales, and finance teams to manage Stripe’s Corporate and User related FX risk. This includes creating pricing models to keep pace with product expansion and developing hedging strategies to mitigate the risks to Stripe’s profitability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe supports global commerce across 135+ currencies including digital assets.As a result, Stripe needs to build and maintain platform systems capable of pricing, estimating and hedging the resulting&amp;nbsp; FX exposures. Grounded in an understanding of FX market conventions and dynamics, you will partner with Engineering, Data Science, Product, and Finance to maintain operational rigor today while shaping long-term pricing and hedging strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor FX risks, execute trades , reconcile position, and attribute costs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build automated risk monitors, alerting tools, and analytical models using SQL and quantitative coding to enable observability and minimize operational toil&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Product and Engineering to guide the design and scaling of core FX infrastructure, trade execution flows, and liquidity provider integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop risk-based FX pricing methodologies across products and currency pairs, factoring in volatility, transaction costs, netting efficiency, and embedded optionality like rate guarantees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design hedging strategies to mitigate FX risks on financial statements while maintaining robust policies, controls, and operational runbooks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in FX, market risk, trading, quantitative research, or treasury operations, with working knowledge of FX market structure and instruments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Python and SQL to build analytics and tools, backed by a strong foundation in statistics, time series, and risk measurement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional attention to detail and a proven ability to turn complex, imperfect datasets into clear insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience using AI tools to streamline analysis and automation, paired with a critical eye for model validation and verification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional collaboration skills, with the ability to turn complex data into clear narratives and escalate issues concisely under time pressure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Economics, Finance, Statistics, Engineering, Computer Science, Math, or Physics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with automated trading and familiarity with option theory and greeks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building data pipelines and systems working alongside technical teams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

