&lt;p&gt;The Account Executive, Product team connects Privy’s technology with companies building new products across fintech and crypto. The team works closely with Product, Engineering, and Go-to-Market partners to understand prospective customers’ needs, shape technical and commercial solutions, and turn market insights into product and sales strategy. Its focus includes priority segments such as neobanking, payments, and brokerages.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Enterprise Account Executive you’ll own complex enterprise sales cycles and help expand Privy’s work with companies across fintech and crypto. You’ll build relationships with senior commercial and technical stakeholders, develop new opportunities, and help refine Privy’s enterprise sales approach. You’ll also contribute to Privy’s global growth strategy and represent the company at industry events.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Head of Go-to-Market (GTM) to build and close a strong pipeline of enterprise prospects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and test outbound campaigns based on market and customer feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a pipeline across multiple ideal customer profiles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build deep expertise in Privy’s products and lead discovery calls with fintech prospects to understand their needs and explain Privy’s value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full sales cycle, from sourcing opportunities through contract close, and serve as the primary commercial contact for prospective customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the Go-to-Market team’s strategy across North America and other global markets, including Latin America, Asia, and Africa.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze market trends and emerging opportunities to inform Privy’s positioning and sales strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Privy at industry events and conferences as a spokesperson for its fintech business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
