&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Executive Programs team builds relationships and experiences that connect senior customer leaders with Stripe’s leadership, products, and strategy. We create forums where executives can exchange ideas, explore the forces shaping their businesses, and give Stripe direct, substantive feedback.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our executive advisory programs are an important part of how Stripe captures the perspectives of executive buyers. The portfolio includes our global Customer Advisory Board as well as regional, segment, and emerging advisory programs. Our goal is to connect these programs into a coherent system that brings the right customer perspectives into Stripe and helps product, marketing, and go-to-market teams act on what we learn.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Head of Executive Advisory Programs, you will define and build Stripe’s approach to executive advisory forums. You will own our existing global Customer Advisory Board and create the framework for launching and scaling complementary regional and segment councils. You will also identify and incubate new advisory programs as Stripe’s priorities and customer base evolve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will connect program strategy with execution: recruiting influential members, shaping agendas with internal partners, delivering white-glove executive experiences, and building a reliable process for capturing and activating customer feedback. You will work closely with leaders across Product, Product Marketing, Events, Sales, and Customer Success to ensure that Stripe’s advisory programs have clear remits, operate as an interconnected portfolio, and inform relevant product and go-to-market decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define Stripe’s global executive advisory strategy, including the purpose, audience, operating model, and relationship between global, regional, segment, and emerging programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and evolve Stripe’s global Customer Advisory Board, including member strategy and recruitment, executive engagement, agenda development, meeting delivery, and year-round programming&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create a repeatable playbook that enables regional and segment teams to build effective advisory councils while maintaining a consistent quality bar and connection to Stripe’s broader program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, launch, and incubate new executive advisory programs that address emerging customer needs and Stripe priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product and Product Marketing leaders to select strategic topics, translate customer priorities into productive discussions, and route resulting insights to the teams that can act on them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional planning across Product, Product Marketing, Sales, Customer Success, and external agencies, establishing clear responsibilities and resolving areas of overlapping ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and measure program impact, including member engagement, the quality and activation of feedback, executive relationship development, and evidence that customer insights are informing Stripe’s decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience building and leading executive advisory boards, councils, or comparable programs for a global business, including setting program strategy and operating the program from recruitment through follow-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build trusted relationships with C-suite and other senior executives and to represent an organization credibly in executive settings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading complex, cross-functional programs and defining clear responsibilities among teams with adjacent or overlapping remits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand technical products and concepts, identify the implications for customers, and connect executive feedback with product and business priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and delivering high-touch executive events with careful attention to the member experience, content, logistics, and follow-through&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building a portfolio of interconnected global, regional, or segment-based advisory programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing systems for synthesizing qualitative customer feedback, routing it to relevant teams, and measuring whether it influenced decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with product, marketing, sales, customer success, solutions, and events teams in a global technology organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with financial infrastructure, payments, software platforms, or another technically complex industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an organized, detail-oriented, and highly collaborative Executive Engagement Marketing Manager for the Americas to lead the operational execution of executive engagement and hospitality programs across the region. This role will translate program strategy into excellent execution by building the systems, communications, tools, tracking, and cross-functional coordination needed to deliver high-touch experiences for senior external audiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with Sales to identify and engage executives from targeted accounts, enable sellers with clear outreach materials and follow-up workflows, and ensure each program has the right operational foundation before, during, and after the event. The successful candidate is comfortable independently managing multiple complex workstreams, navigating ambiguity, and proactively improving how programs operate at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operations and Program Delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently manage the operational planning and execution of a portfolio of executive engagement and hospitality programs across the Americas, including executive dinners, hosted experiences, and sports hospitality programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain detailed program plans, timelines, workback schedules, attendee management processes, event briefs, and cross-functional communication plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Global Experiential Lead and internal stakeholders to translate program objectives, target audiences, and event formats into clear execution plans&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales Enablement and Audience Engagement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Sales and account teams to support the identification, prioritization, and outreach of senior executives at targeted accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and manage seller enablement materials, including invitations, outreach templates, event details, attendee lists, follow-up guidance, and account-specific communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate the end-to-end attendee journey—from invitation strategy and outreach through registration, confirmations, event-day communications, and post-event follow-up&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marketing Operations and Measurement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the event marketing bill of materials, including email journeys, registration or landing pages, attendee communications, and supporting campaign assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Marketing Operations to execute campaigns and workflows that support invitations, registration, attendance, and post-event follow-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Analytics and Program Management to establish consistent tracking, reporting, and measurement for executive engagement programs, aligned with broader marketing standards&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Event Execution and Hospitality&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate operational details across internal teams, agencies, venues, and other partners to ensure programs are delivered reliably and meet Stripe&#39;s brand and hospitality standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure every event delivers a premium, on-brand Stripe experience appropriate for C-suite and senior executive audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support on-site event execution as needed&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build productive working relationships across Experiential, Sales, Regional Marketing, Demand Generation, Marketing Operations, Analytics, Program Management, and external partners, creating clarity around roles, decisions, dependencies, and next steps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate proactively and clearly, particularly when tradeoffs, risks, or changes could affect program delivery or the attendee experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous Improvement and Shared Learning&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify risks, dependencies, and execution gaps early; recommend practical solutions and escalate when broader program decisions are needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capture learnings and maintain repeatable playbooks, templates, and operating practices that improve future program delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use program data, stakeholder feedback, and operational observations to identify opportunities to improve audience targeting, communications, follow-up, and program execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience in event marketing, field marketing, marketing operations, executive programs, hospitality, or a related B2B marketing role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing complex, detail-intensive projects with multiple stakeholders, deadlines, and dependencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to operate independently within a defined area of responsibility, prioritize competing workstreams, and make sound decisions with incomplete information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the judgment to communicate effectively with senior internal stakeholders and external executive audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management skills, including experience developing workback plans, coordinating deliverables, tracking progress, and resolving execution issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong operational and analytical mindset, with experience using program data, stakeholder feedback, and reporting to improve execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to use AI tools to improve efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting executive engagement programs, C-suite events, customer hospitality, hosted dinners, or premium event experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in B2B technology, fintech, enterprise marketing, or a similarly complex go-to-market environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with CRM, marketing automation, event management, and project management tools, such as Salesforce, Splash, Cvent, Asana, or similar platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building scalable marketing processes, playbooks, templates, or reporting frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with event attribution, pipeline workflows, account-based marketing, or executive audience engagement strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Stripe EMEA Marketing team is a dynamic and rapidly growing group dedicated to transforming customers into enthusiastic advocates for Stripe. Collaborating closely with sales, we focus on accelerating the path to purchase and enhancing product adoption among our user base. Our regional marketing efforts involve crafting and executing tailored marketing plans that resonate with local audiences, as well as spearheading our most significant conferences and sponsorships that drive go-to-market success and business growth. Join us and be part of a culture that celebrates teamwork, innovates boldly, and makes a meaningful impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a strategic, results-oriented marketing leader to drive our marketing engine for SMB and Mid-Market segments across EMEA, with an emphasis on Ideal Customer Profiles. This segment represents a massive portion of Europe’s economic fabric and is a critical driver of our ambitions in the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior individual contributor role for someone who thrives at the intersection of strategy, execution, and cross-functional influence. You&#39;ll translate global priorities into locally resonant programs, ensuring that audiences in the SMB and Mid-Market space have high-quality, insight-driven experiences throughout their lifecycle, from early exploration to long-term partnership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is data-driven, has an unbridled passion for working hand-in-hand with regional sales teams to drive successful user outcomes, and is excited about building a high-velocity revenue engine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and execute the EMEA marketing strategy for SMB and Mid-Market segments with an emphasis on Ideal Customer Profiles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own key business and revenue metrics throughout the sales funnel, with a strong emphasis on accelerating pipeline through upsell and cross-sell opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Partner Marketing to create successful co-selling initiatives that extend our reach within the partner and developer ecosystems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute comprehensive full-funnel marketing plans, partnering with digital marketing and demand generation teams to secure high-value deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Sales leadership to align account plans, ensure disciplined lead follow-up, and establish trust as a strategic partner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with EMEA demand generation and product marketing to identify, scope, and produce or localize compelling content and marketing assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track, measure, and communicate program results, continually optimizing for efficiency and scale while seeking to generate new global best practices, and innovate ways to educate a diverse range of personas about the value that Stripe delivers to businesses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of relevant B2B marketing experience in the EMEA technology market, including specific experience with demand generation and field marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of defining and executing B2B marketing strategies that successfully drive metrics, key performance indicators, and pipeline generation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to convey complex topics with simplicity to diverse audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic mindset with strong problem-solving capabilities and a data-driven approach to decision-making, along with a deep understanding of full-funnel journeys and marketing technology like Salesforce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience scaling programs through agency resources and collaborating across key go-to-market stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A startup mentality with a bias to action and the ability to flex in a fast-paced industry and work environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the payments, financial technology, or adjacent industries, or marketing FinTech solutions or to FinTech companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of the payments, financial technology, and ecommerce industries and partner ecosystems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success delivering marketing programs with and through consulting and technology partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Finance and Strategy team is an integral thought partner to Stripe&#39;s core functional leaders. We bring understanding and predictability to Stripe&#39;s bottom-line financials. We work cross-functionally across many surfaces at Stripe and help steward Stripe&#39;s resource investments to improve the durability of our long-term financial performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Finance and Strategy Analyst to join our growing teams on the Go-to-Market (GTM) and Partnerships teams. You&#39;ll help us with the forecasting, budgeting, and reporting for various departments accurately and in a timely manner and deliver improvements in our integrated financial systems with business partners, financial colleagues, and engineers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Leverage your financial background to support and influence key strategic and business decisions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Design and provide analytical rigor to measure efficiency and ROI of investments in headcount and non-headcount expenses&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Drive reporting, process, and discipline for finance routines to shape and influence decision-making (e.g. budget, forecast, monthly reviews, long-range plans)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Build and own models for in-depth analyses, as well as ensure their quality, timeliness, and accuracy&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Define metrics and leading indicators of business performance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Partner with cross-functional teams, such as Data Science, to develop reporting dashboards&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Drive continuous process improvement, standardization, simplification, and reporting enhancements&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• 4–6 years of relevant experience in strategic finance or FP&amp;amp;A&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• B.A. or B.S degree in related field&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• A keen eye for detail and experience building integrated models from scratch (in Excel or other planning applications) • Experience driving and executing on finance processes (e.g. budget, forecast reviews, negotiations)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• A proven ability to build strong collaborative working relationships with business partners&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Excellent communication and organizational skills, both written and verbal&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Experience working at a high-growth technology or financial services company&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Experience managing headcount and operating expenses&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Experience supporting Go-to-Market, Investment Banking, or Product Functions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Oracle, Anaplan, Tableau, or other equivalent application experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Experience with Python or a willingness to learn&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Experience in data visualization and dashboarding&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building an elite team to drive financial insight and strategy at Stripe. The Finance &amp;amp; Strategy team brings understanding and predictability to Stripe’s financials, and we work together with our key business partners to accelerate long term growth for Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with F&amp;amp;S and Business Leaders to drive the long-term success of Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross functionally to identify important strategy questions and answer them with data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build financial forecasts and targets, track performance, and understand deviations from actuals to drive strategy and operational rigor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gain deep knowledge and understanding of Stripe&#39;s business performance across geographies and user segments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define metrics and leading indicators of business performance and partner with the Analytics team to develop tools and dashboards to make these metrics widely accessible across Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7–14 years of experience in a relevant analytical or finance role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intermediate (at a minimum) or advanced knowledge of SQL or Python is required - you must be well versed working with extremely large and complex datasets + extracting insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with financial analysis, financial forecasting, BvA (variance analysis), and other financial concepts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on ambiguous problems and driving solutions/projects independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to automate and use AI to streamline recurring tasks/analyses, in order to free up time to work on more strategic and higher impact work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building dashboards and data visualization tools from scratch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to build strong collaborative working relationships with business partners and department leads. You are seen as a trusted and objective advisor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An enthusiastic &quot;roll up your sleeves&quot; mentality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to be a self-starter capable of driving business results without significant supervision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a global capacity (this team will work will all regions)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Experience in a strategic finance function at a high-growth tech company, preferably in the payments/fintech space&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

