&lt;p&gt;Our ideal Product Manager will be relentlessly user-focused, comfortable in ambiguity,&amp;nbsp;have&amp;nbsp;strong technical skills, and&amp;nbsp;have&amp;nbsp;the desire to create something new&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of managing product managers, 8+ years as a product manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep user empathy and a high bar for user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing a multi-year vision, strategy and roadmap for large scale products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience hiring, managing, and building high-performing customer-focused Product Management teams in multiple continents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading cross-team initiatives from ideation to execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical expertise: You’ve led technical products and/or have a background in computer science (or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Connect Platform&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Connect is Stripe’s platform for businesses that serve other businesses. It helps platforms onboard and verify participants, manage accounts, accept payments, and pay out funds without building payments, compliance, or financial services infrastructure themselves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Connect Risk team builds the risk management capabilities that help platforms operate safely from day one, including onboarding, Know Your Customer (KYC) verification, fraud and credit risk management, and tax reporting. As AI-native platforms and marketplaces emerge, this work helps Stripe support increasingly dynamic global ecosystems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own Connected Account Onboarding Experiences, the products and journeys that help platforms onboard their users safely, compliantly, and with minimal friction. You will shape experiences from sign-up and authentication through readiness to use Stripe products, across application programming interfaces (APIs) and hosted or embedded user interfaces (UI).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will use funnel data, user research, and experimentation to improve conversion while meeting Stripe’s commitments to regulators and financial partners. You will set the strategy for what should be standardized or configurable across platform business models, products, and geographies, including opportunities to use artificial intelligence (AI) and agentic interfaces.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the vision, strategy, goals, and roadmap for Connected Account Onboarding Experiences globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional execution across Connect, Risk, engineering, design, data science, and partner-facing teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use funnel metrics, user research, and experimentation to identify friction and improve onboarding conversion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate risk, regulatory, and partner requirements into intuitive experiences across APIs, platform tools, and connected-account UI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build scalable onboarding foundations that support different platform models, geographies, and evolving AI-enabled experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of product management or product-focused founder experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading complex, multi-quarter product roadmaps and aligning internal teams and external partners around shared goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience partnering with engineering, design, and data teams to build products and systems at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills, including defining success metrics, running experiments, and using data to improve business outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to articulate user problems and product decisions clearly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on complex platform, ecosystem, or regulated products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate with autonomy in a dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in high growth companies and products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, financial technology, or financial infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building user onboarding solutions in enterprise or business-to-business (B2B) industries through APIs or user interfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience redesigning traditional user journeys through AI and building agentic interfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Connect&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While accepting payments on the internet has become easier over the past several years, due in large part to the advent of modern payments APIs, the internet infrastructure for routing these same payments—to suppliers, sellers, partners, service providers, and recipients—remains outdated.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Connect is Stripe’s leading product for marketplaces, on-demand services, ecommerce site builders, invoicing platforms, professional SaaS products, fundraising platforms, rental management platforms, and more. By using Connect, users in each of these categories can link multiple parties to exchange goods or services. These users rely on Connect for the crucial function of routing payments reliably between these parties.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By powering fast, flexible, compliant, and cost-efficient payment routing on the internet, Connect not only spurs the creation of innovative business models but also enables organizations—whether businesses, nonprofits, or government agencies—to bring previously offline payments online.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a chance to define a foundational product area at Stripe. You will turn a fast-changing set of user and product needs into durable platform primitives that work across products, industries, and geographies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role combines high-leverage strategy with hands-on product execution. You will work through ambiguous, consequential questions like: what should a platform be able to model? What should be simple by default but flexible when needed? How can Stripe make complex financial infrastructure feel effortless for a platform and its users?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The outcome of your work will compound. The abstractions you help create will be reused across Connect and Stripe, shaping what new products platforms can build and how quickly they can bring them to market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Product Manager on Stripe’s Connect team, you will shape the strategy and oversee the execution of high-impact initiatives serving modern marketplaces and software platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Product development at Stripe is highly collaborative. You will work closely with engineering, design, analytics, marketing, sales, and customer-facing teams. You will also engage directly with customers and present your plans to Stripe’s leadership team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and advance a compelling product vision for Connect&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Devise the strategy for high-impact initiatives serving modern marketplaces and software platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate product strategy and customer needs into clear product requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee execution across the teams involved in delivering these initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with engineering, design, analytics, marketing, sales, and customer-facing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet with customers to understand their needs and gather feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present product plans to Stripe’s leadership team and incorporate feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;More than three years of product management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A computer science background or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product judgment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to lead products that require coordination across multiple teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Persistence and resourcefulness in driving successful outcomes for products and teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Bridge&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re creating an entirely new payments platform, built with stablecoins, to simplify global money movement. Bridge enables faster, cheaper payments and borderless access to dollars via stablecoins. Through our APIs, businesses can send and receive funds across borders faster and cheaper vs. SWIFT and other fiat-only rails. Our virtual accounts enable international consumers and businesses to easily access, store, and spend US dollars. Our payouts infrastructure enables platforms to disburse USD to anyone globally. We believe many trillions of dollars will move and settle through stablecoin payment rails. Bridge is pulling this future forward.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a small team of people who have previously built financial infrastructure at some of the world&#39;s leading companies (Coinbase, Stripe, Square, Brex, Upstart, DoorDash, Airbnb), and each and every one of them chose Bridge because they fundamentally believe that stablecoins will be a critical piece of financial infrastructure that allows for the improvement of global money movement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join our Product team to build the systems that make global, programmable money trustworthy at scale. At Bridge, we’re not just improving global payments — we’re reinventing how money moves across borders using stablecoins and modern financial infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Product Manager for Developer Experience, you&#39;ll own the end-to-end developer experience from their first encounter with Bridge to transacting billions of dollars in volume on our platform. You&#39;ll work at the intersection of product, engineering, data, and go-to-market to build the self-serve onboarding, developer Dashboard, and activation systems that help any developer build a scaled and successful business with Bridge.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is about enabling a developer of any size and stage to build and scale their business successfully on Bridge.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end developer lifecycle and key products, spanning self-serve sign-up, KYB and onboarding, the developer Dashboard, and activation and retention programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive product features from ideation to launch in close collaboration with engineering, design, data, and go-to-market teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and evolve data-driven signals and systems that recognize what a developer needs at each stage and respond automatically with the right nudges, support, and interventions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own the product roadmap that creates a scalable and intuitive experience for every developer to use Bridge’s full suite products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own key developer metrics (e.g. activation rate, time-to-first-transaction, developer retention) to drive business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with go-to-market and support teams to understand developer feedback and ship improvements rapidly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Need to Thrive&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Empathy for users&lt;/strong&gt;: You’re passionate about uncovering and solving pain points.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep curiosity&lt;/strong&gt;: You never stop asking “why” and dig into both qualitative and quantitative data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Owner’s mentality&lt;/strong&gt;: You tackle challenges head-on and drive solutions with conviction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative spirit&lt;/strong&gt;: You work seamlessly with team members but aren’t afraid to make the call when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clarity and simplicity&lt;/strong&gt;: You translate complex systems into intuitive, straightforward user experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bias for learning&lt;/strong&gt;: You embrace mistakes as opportunities to grow and improve quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6–10+ years of product management experience, with exposure to developer platforms, onboarding, and product-led growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or owning systems related to onboarding, activation, retention, or self-serve growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating across multiple customer segments or go-to-market motions, from self-serve to enterprise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working with APIs, dashboards, or developer-facing platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fintech, payments, or crypto.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re ready to shape the future of how money moves, we want to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies — from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups — use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Ecosystem Risk Product Management team sits at the intersection of growth and protection. Our focus is twofold. We enable online businesses—including those in emerging and regulated industries—to start and grow on Stripe, while protecting consumers, merchants, and partners from financial crimes. We build financial infrastructure at scale that powers every transaction on Stripe, deliver merchant-facing UI and API experiences, and develop AI-driven solutions to some of the hardest and most exciting challenges in the digital economy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the vision and multi-year roadmap for AI-powered financial crimes controls—spanning detection, investigation, information collection, and the UI and API surfaces that tie them together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build core infrastructure that underpins Stripe&#39;s growing suite of products and services. • Develop investigator tools that power accurate case reviews using the best of AI and human expertise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cross-functional execution by partnering closely with engineering, operations, design, data science, go-to-market, legal, and product teams across Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own success metrics, navigate complex trade-offs, drive prioritization, and measure outcomes with rigor to demonstrate impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align leadership and stakeholders by synthesizing input from across the organization and external sources, and communicating a clear point of view to peers and executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor the external landscape—regulatory trends, emerging technologies, and competitive offerings—to inform strategy and identify opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years in Product Management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience building infrastructure and user experiences at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of operating effectively in highly cross-functional environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical, problem-solving, and decision-making skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in financial crimes or fraud prevention within financial services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies — from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups — use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to grow the GDP of the internet, and we won&#39;t stop until we&#39;ve made it easy for any business anywhere to participate in the digital economy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Governments around the world are fundamentally changing how businesses report and exchange transactions. Continuous Transaction Controls (CTC) and e-invoicing mandates — now active or imminent in France, Germany, Spain, Poland, and across Latin America — require businesses to transmit structured invoice data through certified government networks in real time. For Stripe&#39;s global user base, compliant e-invoicing is rapidly becoming a prerequisite for conducting commerce, not a nice-to-have.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re building the e-invoicing infrastructure that makes this invisible for Stripe users. That means embedding compliant invoice generation, validation, and transmission directly into Stripe Billing and Invoicing — abstracting the full complexity of regional mandates and network certification behind a seamless product experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact, greenfield role. You&#39;ll own Stripe&#39;s e-invoicing product end-to-end: setting the strategy, driving execution, and making Stripe the go-to solution for businesses navigating the global shift to real-time invoicing compliance. You&#39;ll work at the intersection of product, engineering, partnerships, and go-to-market — and you&#39;ll be laying the foundation for a capability that will matter to every Stripe user operating in a mandated market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the e-invoicing product vision and roadmap, translating complex and evolving regulatory requirements into a coherent multi-year strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive Stripe&#39;s expansion across mandated global markets (France, Germany, Spain, Poland) and into Latin America, sequencing coverage pragmatically against enforcement timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead build, buy, and partner decisions — evaluating the right combination of internal investment and external capabilities to meet compliance deadlines without sacrificing long-term product quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own the end-to-end user journey: from onboarding (including business identity verification) to live invoice transmission via certified networks like Peppol&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the Billing, Invoicing, Tax, and Connect teams to embed e-invoicing as a native part of Stripe&#39;s financial infrastructure — not a bolted-on feature&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish quality, reliability, and activation metrics that hold every component of the e-invoicing stack accountable, and use those metrics to drive continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with GTM, Sales, and Solutions Engineering to position Stripe as the leading e-invoicing solution for upmarket and enterprise customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Stripe credibly with regulators, certification bodies, and industry partners as we build direct relationships with key tax authorities and networks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of product management experience, with at least 2 years in a B2B fintech, payments, tax, or compliance-adjacent product domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep familiarity with the e-invoicing landscape — you understand CTC frameworks, structured invoice formats (Factur-X, XRechnung, PEPPOL BIS), and the regulatory dynamics driving mandates in Europe and Latin America&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical fluency: you can credibly partner with engineers on API design, data schemas, and network integration architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to run a build/buy/partner analysis and translate the output into concrete roadmap decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience launching products across multiple markets simultaneously, including navigating localization, regulatory compliance, and differing user needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent cross-functional leadership — you get things done across Engineering, Legal, Finance, and GTM without formal authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, direct communication: you can distill a complex compliance landscape into a compelling product narrative for both internal stakeholders and external audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating third-party technology providers or acquisitions into a core product platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Stripe Billing, Invoicing, or Tax products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience building toward Peppol access point certification or direct integrations with national tax authority platforms (e.g., Chorus Pro, KSeF)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to B2B invoicing workflows in mid-market or enterprise contexts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this role, why now&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;E-invoicing is one of the most consequential shifts in global business compliance in a decade, and Stripe is early in building the infrastructure to make it effortless. You&#39;ll have the mandate, the resources, and the cross-functional backing to build something significant — and the chance to make Stripe synonymous with world-class e-invoicing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is an equal opportunity employer. We look for people with exceptional abilities, who are excited by hard problems and big opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Financial Systems organization partners with Stripe’s People organization to build trusted, intuitive products for employees, managers, and People professionals. We aim to make routine interactions simple and self-service while ensuring that work requiring judgment or care reaches the right person with the right context.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our products connect data, knowledge, workflows, and systems that span the employee experience. We are building toward a future in which employees and managers can get accurate answers and complete common tasks without navigating fragmented tools, while People teams can spend more time on the work that benefits most from&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own products that make it easier for employees to get accurate guidance and complete common People-related tasks, while helping People team focus their expertise on work that requires judgment and care. You will identify the highest-impact user problems, define the product strategy and roadmap, and lead products from discovery through delivery, adoption, and iteration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to shape a growing product area at the intersection of employee experience, enterprise systems, data, and applied AI. You will help develop agentic products that connect people to accurate guidance, automate appropriate actions, and help People practitioners focus their expertise where it matters most. Success requires understanding the capabilities and limitations of AI and machine learning when applied to business-critical, regulated, and strictly governed problems. You will also use AI-enabled tools throughout the product development lifecycle to accelerate discovery, prototyping, requirements development, evaluation, and iteration while protecting employee trust.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of employees, managers, and People practitioners, then translate their most important needs into a focused product roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own products end to end, from problem discovery and strategy through delivery, adoption, measurement, and iteration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design coherent experiences that connect fragmented data, knowledge, workflows, and systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with the People org, engineering, data, security, legal, and others to make sound product and architecture tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define measures to understand adoption, engagement, and impact for products and develop insights into the metrics to guide improvements to the product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop agentic People products and define where systems may recommend, act, escalate, or defer to accountable human judgment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI-enabled tools throughout product development and help establish effective practices for AI-assisted discovery, prototyping, specification, testing, and iteration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead adoption and establish sustainable ownership and support for products that change established ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of product management or equivalent experience leading the development of software products for internal or external users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience independently navigating ambiguity, identifying the underlying user problem, and converting broad strategies into focused product roadmaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shipping products that connect workflows, data, and multiple systems or teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical understanding of AI and machine-learning product development beyond using LLM-based tools, including model capabilities, data requirements, evaluation methods, failure modes, privacy considerations, and the tradeoffs between probabilistic, deterministic, and human-led approaches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI-enabled tools to improve the quality and speed of product discovery, prototyping, delivery, or evaluation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead across functions and build alignment among stakeholders with different expertise, incentives, and responsibilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing products where user trust, privacy, permissions, or other sensitive requirements are central to the product experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with employee products, human-resources technology, People operations, enterprise workflow, or manager-facing tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building governed data products, self-service experiences, or role-aware applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shipping agentic or AI/ML-powered products for People or another trust-sensitive domain, with appropriate evaluation, privacy safeguards, escalation, and human accountability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading adoption and organizational change for products that replace established manual processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is open to remote candidates located anywhere within the Eastern Time Zone.&amp;nbsp; Global Payouts empowers Stripe users to move money effortlessly, quickly, and securely to anyone, anywhere. Businesses rely on us to distribute billions of dollars to employees, contractors, sellers, and claimants across our Dashboard, APIs, and platform integrations via Financial Accounts.We are gaining rapid momentum across both self-serve and enterprise segments. Our demand spans high-growth fintechs, leading AI platforms, and some of the world&#39;s largest marketplaces.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are now entering a decisive phase of expansion. Over the next 12–18 months, the capabilities we build robust cross-border infrastructure, advanced enterprise controls, and tailored vertical-specific features will determine whether Global Payouts becomes the definitive default for businesses distributing money at scale. This role sits at the absolute center of that mission.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an entrepreneurial Product Manager to spearhead our cross-border expansion and enterprise capabilities. This is a high-impact, broad-scope role where you will set the strategic vision and drive execution across two pillars essential to our hyper-growth:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-border: You will expand the reach and competitive edge of our cross-border infrastructure by building out rate locking, local bank account coverage, and cross-border card rails. Crucially, you will lead the productization of fee passthrough—translating a bespoke solution originally built for a major AI platform into a broadly available, highly scalable capability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enterprise: You will define and deliver the advanced controls, reporting, and billing features required by sophisticated, high-volume operators. This includes recipient tax reporting, two-step confirmation workflows, enterprise billing models (e.g., IC+, platform fees), and robust security access controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Across both domains, you will partner directly with Sales, Partnerships, and Go-to-Market (GTM) teams to convert active enterprise demand into durable product investments, developing industry-specific capabilities for key verticals like remittance and fintech.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cross-Border Expansion&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the roadmap for global payout infrastructure, prioritizing rate locking, local bank coverage, and cross-border card rails.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Productize fee passthrough, transforming a custom integration into a scalable, self-serve offering to drive rapid adoption among new users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design industry-specific solutions for high-value verticals (e.g., remittance, fintech) rooted in deep user research and strategic GTM alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Enterprise Capabilities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship enterprise-grade controls and reporting tools, including recipient tax reporting, two-step confirmation workflows, and advanced security access controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect enterprise billing primitives—such as Interchange Plus (IC+) and platform fees—to enable flexible, scalable commercial models for large payout operators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cross-Functional Leadership&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales and Partnerships to support active enterprise deals and PUA requests, distilling bespoke client requirements into scalable, prioritized product investments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate seamlessly across Financial Accounts, Connect, and the broader money movement platform to ensure new capabilities integrate cleanly and compound in value over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and track success metrics, holding yourself accountable to measurable adoption targets across both self-serve and enterprise segments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Who you are&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is open to remote candidates located anywhere within the Eastern Time Zone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of product management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to own a product area end-to-end—defining strategy, driving execution, and measuring outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shipping products that serve multiple user segments or operate across significant technical or regulatory complexity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to work with Sales, GTM, or enterprise customers and translate their needs into scalable product investments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical instincts: comfort with data, metrics, and building the measurement framework before you ship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written communication: crisp specs, clear PRDs, and the ability to build alignment across functions and levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, fintech, financial infrastructure, or other regulated industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background working on enterprise or B2B products with complex commercial or compliance requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience productizing bespoke or custom solutions into broadly available features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe Terminal helps businesses extend their online presence into the physical world. Our mission is to make it as easy for businesses to accept in-person payments as Stripe has made it to accept payments online.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Terminal provides an integrated in-person payments platform spanning software, payment processing, device fleet management, and hardware. Our hardware portfolio includes Stripe-designed readers and accessories as well as devices from third-party hardware partners. Together, these products enable businesses to build reliable, differentiated in-person payment experiences across a broad range of use cases, countries, and operating environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an experienced Product Manager to build the strategy, development, and expansion of Terminal’s hardware portfolio. This role will work across both first-party and third-party hardware, helping define the multi-year roadmap for the devices, accessories, and partner ecosystem that power Terminal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will partner closely with hardware engineering, firmware and software engineering, design, operations, logistics, partnerships, sales, finance, legal, and regional teams. This is a highly cross-functional role for someone who can connect customer needs, technical constraints, business strategy, and execution across user experience, device capabilities, cost, quality, reliability, supply, and time to market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and execute a multi-year strategy and roadmap for Terminal hardware across Stripe-built devices, third-party devices, accessories, and emerging form factors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a clear point of view on where Stripe should build, partner, or expand its hardware portfolio to address customer needs, competitive gaps, and global market opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define product requirements, user journeys, and acceptance criteria for end-to-end hardware products from concept through validation, launch, and post-launch iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with hardware, firmware, software, and quality engineering teams to guide development and deliver high-quality device experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with external OEM, ODM, and technology partners to evaluate product capabilities, define joint roadmaps, resolve technical issues, and deliver hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the continued global expansion of Terminal’s third-party hardware portfolio, including device availability, local payment-method support, certifications, distribution, pricing, and launch readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and lead the evaluation process for additional third-party hardware providers and build business cases for new device categories, accessories, connectivity, and specialized use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage directly with Terminal users, sales teams, and partners to understand in-person payments workflows, product gaps, and opportunities to improve the device experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish success metrics for hardware products and partnerships, using customer feedback, adoption, device reliability, support signals, and financial performance to inform decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate product strategy, priorities, risks, and trade-offs clearly to cross-functional partners and Stripe leadership, traveling occasionally to partner sites or Stripe offices, including APAC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of product management experience or equivalent experience leading complex technology products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success shipping physical hardware, connected devices, embedded products, payments devices, consumer electronics, or similarly complex products from concept through launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining and driving product strategy, roadmaps, requirements, prioritization, and launch plans for technical products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering closely with hardware, firmware, and software engineering teams and the ability to participate credibly in technical product and architecture discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment in navigating trade-offs across customer experience, technical feasibility, reliability, quality, cost, supply, and launch timing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with hardware product-development and manufacturing processes, including prototype development, validation, production readiness, and sustaining lifecycle management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with external vendors, manufacturers, OEMs, ODMs, or other strategic technology partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A customer-focused and analytical approach to product development, with experience leading cross-functional programs, creating alignment, and using evidence to set priorities and measure outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, commerce platforms, point-of-sale systems, or in-person payments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a portfolio that includes both first-party products and third-party partner products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with sourcing, supply-chain risk, device pricing, unit economics, and global distribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payment-device certifications, local payment methods, accessibility requirements, connectivity, or regulated hardware environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience launching products internationally or a technical background in electrical engineering, computer science, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;IAM is the nerve center of Stripe. We control how millions of businesses grant access to their account, including employees, AI agents, apps, and API integrations, across the Dashboard, API, CLI, and MCP. We&#39;re also a platform team, building the unified, fine-grained permissions model that every product at Stripe builds on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI agents are changing how businesses operate, and how they get authorized, governed, and secured is being defined right now—largely by us. We’re tackling challenging and unsolved problems for real businesses, like how to model agents when they blur the line between acting on behalf of a human vs. standalone principals, or how to authorize entire agent workflows rather than step-by-step actions. We’re collaborating directly with the frontier AI labs on the evolution of MCP, new identity protocols, and agent integrations. We build for solo founders and Fortune 500s alike, and the tension between those two is where the real product work lives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll set the vision and drive the roadmap for how every principal, human, agent, or app, gets access to a Stripe account. You&#39;ll do it by talking directly to the founders, admins, and developers who use it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design the experience of granting access, everywhere.&lt;/strong&gt; Signing up, inviting a teammate, creating an API key, authorizing an agent or a third-party app.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design for agents specifically.&lt;/strong&gt; Design for agents as a new principal within Stripe, including how they authenticate, what they&#39;re allowed to do, and how businesses stay in control, including approvals and human-in-the-loop checkpoints for actions involving real money. You&#39;re defining an experience that will set the industry standard.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive least privilege, made easy.&lt;/strong&gt; Take holistic ownership across Stripe to ensure that every user, app and agent has only the permissions it requires. Build custom roles, smart permission defaults, and permission recommendations based on real API usage to make least-privilege authorization easy rather than tedious.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Push toward a world without secrets.&lt;/strong&gt; Make secretless authentication (Workload Identity Federation) the default way developers integrate with Stripe to prevent emerging security threats from increasingly sophisticated and AI-powered attackers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner across all of Stripe.&lt;/strong&gt; Pitch an ambitious vision, then get teams across Dashboard, API Platform, Security, Payments and Money Movement genuinely excited to build it with you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The hardest part of this job, and the most fun, is the constant trade-off: usability vs. security, flexibility vs. simplicity. It takes taste to find a shape that feels effortless for a solo founder and holds up at Fortune 500 scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in PM, shipping platform or infrastructure products that other teams build on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in security, identity, auth, or developer platforms, or serious curiosity about the space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A habit of talking to users to find the real problem, not the reported one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency to go deep with engineers on authorization and authentication design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bias toward experimentation over big-bang launches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort setting direction in a space that&#39;s still being invented, across teams you don&#39;t manage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Bridge&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re creating an entirely new payments platform, built with stablecoins, to simplify global money movement. Bridge enables faster, cheaper payments and borderless access to dollars via stablecoins. Through our APIs, businesses can send and receive funds across borders faster and cheaper vs. SWIFT and other fiat-only rails. Our virtual accounts enable international consumers and businesses to easily access, store, and spend US dollars. Our payouts infrastructure enables platforms to disburse USD to anyone globally. We believe many trillions of dollars will move and settle through stablecoin payment rails. Bridge is pulling this future forward.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a small team of people who have previously built financial infrastructure at some of the world&#39;s leading companies (Coinbase, Stripe, Square, Brex, Upstart, DoorDash, Airbnb), and each and every one of them chose Bridge because they fundamentally believe that stablecoins will be a critical piece of financial infrastructure that allows for the improvement of global money movement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join our Issuance Product team to shape the future of financial access and infrastructure. We&#39;re not just improving global payments, we&#39;re reinventing them with modern rails that allow for fast, cheap transactions at any size. You will build a platform that powers issuing compliant stablecoins in US/EU and beyond. We work with some of the largest fintechs, crypto companies, blockchains and more. This is your chance to lead meaningful innovation from day one, redefining the way businesses and people exchange value globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a world class issuance platform that has the scale to power billions of dollars of transactions and issued stablecoins. Product areas include liquidity delivery, reserves management, mint/burn infrastructure, rewards, on-chain/crypto smart contracts, and launching custom stablecoins.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive product features from ideation to launch, collaborating with designers, engineers, and cross-functional partners such as legal and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of our users’ needs, operational landscape, and competitive environment&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;across international markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own outcomes end-to-end, using data, feedback, and rapid iteration to refine your approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make tough prioritization calls, balancing user needs, technical feasibility, and business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive high-traffic features at scale, ensuring security, speed, and reliability for millions of users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Need to Thrive&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Empathy for users&lt;/strong&gt;: You’re passionate about uncovering and solving pain points.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep curiosity&lt;/strong&gt;: You never stop asking “why” and dig into both qualitative and quantitative data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Owner’s mentality&lt;/strong&gt;: You tackle challenges head-on and drive solutions with conviction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative spirit&lt;/strong&gt;: You work seamlessly with team members but aren’t afraid to make the call when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clarity and simplicity&lt;/strong&gt;: You translate complex systems into intuitive, straightforward user experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bias for learning&lt;/strong&gt;: You embrace mistakes as opportunities to grow and improve quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in product management or a related role, with a proven record of delivering impactful products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success working with engineers, designers, and external partners to build complex systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen and comfort navigating ecosystem and platform-level challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating APIs, managing developer platforms, or building ecosystem-driven products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building regulated infrastructure in fintech, payments, or crypto.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re ready to shape the future of how money moves, we want to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Link team builds the premier consumer network for next-generation commerce, leveraging our base of 300M+ registered consumers to pioneer the future of Identity, Consumer Finance, and AI-driven transactions. While our foundation was built on high-conversion merchant payments and a flexible digital wallet, we are expanding far beyond. We are building the infrastructure for a world where AI agents transact on your behalf, stablecoins go mainstream, and identity dictates how money moves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We think of Link as the wallet for the internet — and we&#39;re building for what&#39;s next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will build the Link App experience across web and native — building the wallet product consumers need to feel confident, excited, and inspired by the new ways payments and identity are changing online.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That means being a true champion of the consumer: end-to-end owner of core features, a cross-functional partner to Engineering, Design, and GTM, and an active voice in shaping Link&#39;s consumer strategy alongside Link leadership. You&#39;ll define, build, and scale new and existing products — informed by consumer insights and data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a technical PM who operates with a high degree of autonomy and drive. You care deeply about craft and impact — the only thing that really matters to you is getting well-built products into users&#39; hands. You&#39;re probably already exploring how AI is changing how products get built and what it means for the PM role; you might even have a few half-finished side projects that prove it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the consumer perspective — spend time with users, partner closely with Engineering, GTM, and Operations, and synthesize feedback and market signals into clear product direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the voice of the Link consumer, both within the team and across Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and drive an ambitious roadmap, from expanding core capabilities to leading nascent initiatives through to maturity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish team pace, clear prioritization, and rigorous execution standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner deeply with Engineering, Design, Data Science, Marketing, Sales, and Operations to ship cohesive, frictionless experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in a product or technical role, with experience shipping world-class consumer products at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High taste, design empathy, and sharp judgment — can put yourself in the shoes of consumers and be a steward of crafting great experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rigorous with data — comfortable digging into metrics, writing SQL when needed, and thinking from first principles to deliver the right results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Desire for continuous product improvement; able to optimize for shipping a portfolio of small, medium, and large releases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership mindset — works on whatever it takes to solve problems and delight consumers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication, with a talent for distilling user problems into precise, actionable framing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing high-stakes external partnerships — aligning on milestones and executing integrations end-to-end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives with a high level of autonomy and responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on consumer financial products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building brand new products or working in a startup environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with GTM teams to bring a new product to market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
