&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in high-growth technology or fintech environments&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep cross-functional partnership: Prior experience working alongside Engineering, Product, Legal, Compliance, and GTM/Sales&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data fluency: Experience leveraging data visualization tools and analytical frameworks to back up strategic decisions and measure program success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Stripe Security team is dedicated to improving the security of Stripe and its users. Our users trust us with some of their most sensitive information, and we make security a first-class consideration in everything we do. Security concerns are ever-evolving, creating an extremely dynamic environment for the Security team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Security Governance, Risk, and Compliance (SGRC) team at Stripe provides security governance, risk management, and compliance capabilities to allow Stripe to make strategic security decisions, measure our risk and control posture, and represent Stripe Security to internal and external entities. The successful operation of our organization accelerates Stripe by optimizing the communication and expectations of our security program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Security GRC Program Manager with deep expertise in security compliance to serve as the primary interface between Stripe&#39;s Security organization and external auditors, regulators, and compliance stakeholders. In this role, you&#39;ll represent the Security team in audit engagements, articulate how Stripe&#39;s security controls are designed and how they operate, and ensure that compliance obligations across a complex global regulatory landscape are met with consistency and rigor.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will act as a proxy between external entities like regulators and auditors, and our internal security teams, ensuring consistency in compliance responses and helping maintain a lean and effective compliance program. The ideal candidate is adaptable and finds structure in an evolving and maturing organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as an information security subject matter expert during cross-functional audit engagements, representing the Security team in walkthrough meetings with auditors and regulators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the internal liaison (proxy) between&amp;nbsp; and the Security organization to ensure audits are managed effectively and consistently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain a central repository of audit evidence artifacts required for compliance with SOC 2, PCI DSS, SOX, and other global regulatory standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform security risk and control assessments against common frameworks to ensure compliance with Stripe&#39;s Information Security Policy and Standards and applicable regulations (e.g., ISO 2700x, PCI DSS, SOX, NIST, COBIT)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support control owners with guidance on security control design and redesign to ensure continued compliance and effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate security compliance support for Stripe&#39;s legal entities with regulatory obligations, and collaborate with cross-functional stakeholders to track and report on control remediation efforts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support broader GRC team program initiatives, including policy writing, security awareness training, and third-party security risk assessments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subject matter expert in information security frameworks, practices, policies, standards, and procedures (e.g., NIST CSF, SOC 2, PCI DSS, ISO 27001/2, or equivalent)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in Security Governance, Risk, and Compliance or Technology Compliance roles with a strong understanding of audit processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to global regulatory requirements (e.g., DORA, FFIEC, EBA, NYDFS) and experience integrating them into compliance programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting security audits and supporting compliance across complex, overlapping regulatory frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong program management skills with proficiency in coordinating security assessments and managing multiple stakeholder engagements across time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, with the ability to build relationships at all levels and translate technical security concepts for auditors, regulators, and executive audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Total Rewards Strategy &amp;amp; Enablement (TR S&amp;amp;E) team translates people strategy into business impact, building the infrastructure, programs, and systems that make Total Rewards work at scale. We bridge strategy and execution, partnering with People leadership and cross-functional teams across Finance, Legal, and the business to turn ambiguous problems into durable programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a collaborative, action-oriented Project Manager to join the Total Rewards Strategy and Enablement team. In this role, you’ll lead business-critical People projects, with a primary focus on mergers and acquisitions (M&amp;amp;A).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bringing an acquired business into Stripe requires coordinated work across Total Rewards, People Partners, Recruiting, People Operations, Legal, Finance, and Corporate Development. You’ll project manage the People workstream from diligence and integration planning through close and post-close execution. You’ll turn deal-specific decisions into clear plans, ownership, milestones, and risk-management approaches.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll coordinate functional owners across People workstreams, establish plans and dependencies, and step into the work when needed to unblock progress or close critical gaps. Your work will support transaction timelines, reduce business disruption, and create a consistent experience for acquired Stripes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll build People M&amp;amp;A’s capabilities through repeatable playbooks, infrastructure, and cross-training. This individual contributor role is well suited to someone who can bring structure to ambiguity and move between strategy and execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project manage People M&amp;amp;A workstreams &lt;/strong&gt;from diligence and planning through close and post-close execution. Workstreams may include organizational alignment, employee data, onboarding, recruiting, and people program integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Serve as a central coordination point &lt;/strong&gt;across Total Rewards, People Partners, People Operations, People Systems, Recruiting, People Support, Corporate Development, Legal, Finance, and Corporate Technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Align plans, dependencies, decisions, and accountability &lt;/strong&gt;with transaction timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop and run integration and change-management plans &lt;/strong&gt;that give functional leads, acquired Stripes, and other affected audiences the information and support they need at each stage of a transaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Identify cross-functional dependencies, risks, and blockers early. &lt;/strong&gt;Coordinate resolution and escalate issues when needed to protect integration timelines and the Stripe experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Establish feedback and support mechanisms for acquired Stripes&lt;/strong&gt;, including surveys, office hours, and centralized support channels. Use feedback to improve integration plans and change-management approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and improve People M&amp;amp;A’s infrastructure&lt;/strong&gt;, including project plans, templates, checklists, playbooks, reporting, and retrospective documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build capability across People workstreams &lt;/strong&gt;through documentation, cross-training, and shared practices that support more consistent future integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support other business-critical and transformational projects &lt;/strong&gt;across Total Rewards and the People team as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 7+ years of project or program management experience at a global company, including 2+ years project managing workstreams within the M&amp;amp;A lifecycle, including diligence, integration planning, close readiness, and post-close integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience leading complex, cross-functional programs from planning through execution and building repeatable program infrastructure, such as integration playbooks, project-plan templates, readiness checklists, risk logs, or retrospective processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a track record of turning ambiguous problems into structured, repeatable programs. You’re comfortable building new programs in a scaling environment while improving and standardizing how work gets done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have excellent written and verbal communication skills. You can write a one-page executive update, a decision memo tailored to stakeholders, and a step-by-step operator playbook with equal fluency. You guide project teams through complex work in a direct, approachable, and inclusive way.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can manage senior cross-functional stakeholders across Total Rewards, People Partners, People Systems, Recruiting, Corporate Development, Legal, and Finance. You know when to build alignment, raise a risk, and escalate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re comfortable working with data and systems such as Workday and Greenhouse. You use data to clarify decisions, communicate recommendations, and define requirements with People Systems partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You focus on the experience of acquired Stripes and the teams operating the program, not only on program artifacts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can manage competing priorities and adapt in a fast-paced environment. You work effectively independently and across teams, bring structure to complexity, and follow through on the details that make a program successful.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with change management frameworks, such as the Prosci ADKAR Model, and applying them to employee or operational change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project or program management certification or training, such as Project Management Professional (PMP), Lean, Six Sigma, or a comparable methodology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Total Rewards Strategy &amp;amp; Enablement (TR S&amp;amp;E) team translates people strategy into business impact, building the infrastructure, programs, and systems that make Total Rewards work at scale. We&#39;re a small, high-leverage team that bridges strategy and execution, partnering with People leadership and cross-functional teams across Finance, Legal, and the business to turn ambiguous problems into durable programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s Total Rewards programs span compensation, benefits, equity, internal mobility/immigration, and mergers and acquisitions (M&amp;amp;A), each with cross-functional dependencies, regulatory stakes, and direct impact on the Stripes they affect. Delivering these programs well takes a Project Manager who develops real subject matter depth, engages with pillar leads as a strategic partner, and brings structure to decisions that aren&#39;t always clear-cut.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring a &lt;strong&gt;Project Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to own high-priority Total Rewards projects and programs end to end. You&#39;ll work closely with our Benefits, Compensation, Equity, Talent Mobility, and M&amp;amp;A pillars, building expertise in how these programs work and what it takes to land them well. Some programs have established playbooks you&#39;ll sharpen; others are less defined and will need you to help shape the approach before you execute it. Across all of them, you&#39;ll identify dependencies early, proactively surface and mitigate risks, and keep complex, multi-stakeholder work moving toward clear outcomes. This is a high-leverage individual contributor role for someone who brings both rigor and judgment to every project they own.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end project management for high-profile cyclical and transformational Total Rewards projects, from intake and scoping through go-live and handoff to program owners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise and embed with project teams across the Total Rewards and People portfolio, raising the quality bar and building PM capability across the extended team, not just doing the work yourself&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build subject matter expertise across Benefits, Compensation, Equity, Talent Mobility, and M&amp;amp;A — becoming a reliable strategic thought partner to pillar teams on program decisions, not just a tracker of status&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, automate, and continuously improve the infrastructure that makes program management repeatable and scalable: intake frameworks, project plan templates, SOPs, playbooks, and handoff checklists for common program types&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage AI tools in your daily work and the team&#39;s workflows, using them to accelerate synthesis, drafting, stakeholder communications, and documentation, and actively identifying new opportunities to work faster and better&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cross-functional alignment across People and key partner functions (Legal, Finance, Corporate Technology, and others), creating shared visibility into priorities, dependencies, and blockers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tackle complex, ambiguous program questions with rigor and independence, owning work from problem definition through final recommendation — including defining the approach, monitoring progress, identifying risks early, and putting mitigation in place before issues land&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Surface patterns and gaps across the program portfolio, translating observations into structured analysis and recommendations for People leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of People project, program, or operations management experience, including at least 3 years driving multi-stakeholder, cross-functional programs end to end, ideally at a scaling or global company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building from scratch: you&#39;ve created processes, playbooks, or program infrastructure where none existed before, not just improved what was already in place&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written communication: you can produce an executive update, a stakeholder decision memo, and a practitioner playbook with equal fluency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management across senior cross-functional partners: you drive results with a balance of urgency and thoughtfulness, and know when to push, when to align, and when to escalate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI expertise: you default to AI tools for synthesis, drafting, analysis, and communications, and you proactively design workflows that help the team move faster and operate at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical fluency: you can work with data to build a credible narrative, identify patterns across a program portfolio, and make recommendations grounded in evidence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A users-first mindset: you obsess over the Stripe employee experience and the operator experience, not just the project/program artifacts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with change management frameworks (such as Prosci ADKAR) and judgment about when to apply structured change management vs. lighter-touch approaches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and deploying enablement materials or training resources for cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Total Rewards, People Operations, or an adjacent HR domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with PM and collaboration tools (Asana, Jira, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Total Rewards or HR systems (such as Workday, equity administration platforms, or benefits administration tools)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PMP, Lean/Six Sigma, or comparable structured-program training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At its core, Stripe is a treasury company. We are seeking someone great to join our Treasury Finance Transformation team to help us fulfill our mission of building the Global Payments and Treasury Network (GPTN). In order to continue to build novel and powerful products for our users, our own treasury capabilities must be excellent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Treasury Finance Transformation team comprises execution and delivery experts dedicated to supporting, building, and expanding our treasury capabilities from the ground up. We play a crucial role in analyzing large datasets, evaluating business processes to shape our vision, and driving strategic decision-making to influence business outcomes through cross-functional collaboration. As a project manager on the team, you will ensure seamless coordination and execution by aligning team efforts, managing timelines, and delivering on objectives, ultimately optimizing the efficiency and success of our transformation initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an experienced PM to play an integral role to lead and drive towards solutions as we develop sophisticated Treasury Finance capabilities. You will primarily support the Capital Markets and FX teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tackle hard, ambiguous questions with rigor and independence, owning projects from problem definition to final recommendation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and manage complex projects primarily focused on operational efficiency, governance, and regulatory compliance, ensuring alignment with organizational standards and regulatory requirements across multiple jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement project plans, optimize workflows, and ensure all stakeholders are informed and engaged throughout the process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional teams, including legal, finance, and engineering, to assess the impact of operational and regulatory changes and identify areas for improvement in processes and controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor project progress, identify potential risks, and proactively implement mitigation strategies to ensure timely and successful project delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain effective project governance, ensuring that all project activities, decisions, and key milestones comply with standards and best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare materials to present to senior management, internal and external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of 6 years of experience in Change Management, gained in management consulting or change management within high-growth tech companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead complex, cross-functional projects involving multiple stakeholders across various functional areas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills with a keen eye for detail, and the ability to understand complex technical products and articulate their value to non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on, adaptable approach with comfort operating in ambiguous environments, taking on varied roles, and collaborating effectively with senior management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity-driven mindset to effectively lead technical teams and subject matter experts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of the payments industry and fintech landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with capital markets and risk management concepts such as financing, investments, and hedging risks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing complex business and data requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SQL, Python, or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI as an enabler of change management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Recruiting Strategy &amp;amp; Enablement Team is dedicated to enhancing the quality and efficiency of Stripe&#39;s Recruiting function. By executing a suite of strategic projects and programs, we optimize the caliber and productivity of our global recruiting team. Our focus includes driving programmatic initiatives, facilitating data-informed decision-making, and steering change management to enable robust business engagement. We are looking for a talented project manager to join our team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Project Manager on the Recruiting Strategy &amp;amp; Enablement team, you&#39;ll own strategic programs end-to-end — from scoping and stakeholder alignment through execution, enablement, and measurement. You&#39;ll partner closely with Global Recruiting Leads, Hiring Managers, and cross-functional teams to ship initiatives that improve recruiting quality, efficiency, and compliance at a global scale. Day-to-day, you&#39;ll balance long-running portfolio work with fast-moving priorities that require you to ramp quickly and execute with minimal oversight.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and steer strategic programs&#39; objectives and key result areas, including tracking and reporting metrics and overall program management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead change management initiatives within our recruiting teams and collaborate with partners to facilitate seamless transitions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive enablement strategies that support program adoption, including comms plans, FAQs, and stakeholder-facing resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and implement operational improvements across recruiting programs and processes, maximizing their effectiveness and efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design training guides and educational materials to enhance the skill set of recruiters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Global Recruiting Leads and Hiring Managers to pinpoint and execute high-priority initiatives that elevate our recruiting efforts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage portfolio-level governance: run SteerCos, track workstream DRIs, synthesize progress, and report to leadership on program health and outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate global regulatory and compliance requirements that impact recruiting processes (e.g., pay transparency, pre-employment checks, data privacy), partnering with legal, HR compliance, and People Partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Absorb emerging work as priorities shift — such as hiring sprints, organizational transitions, or rapid-turnaround projects — with minimal ramp time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven expertise in program, change, and project management within a dynamic, global, high-growth environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning and launching strategic programs that drive measurable quality and efficiency improvements in a People or HR function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building, launching, or managing AI-powered programs or assessments — not just personal AI tool use, but owning the strategy, piloting, and rollout of AI-enabled workflows or products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated initiative, autonomy, and critical thinking with keen attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to influence senior leaders and drive alignment across multiple teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
