&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Product and Risk Data Engineering is Stripe&#39;s single source of truth data engineering layer for Payments, Risk, and Product — we enable Stripe to confidently run, measure, and grow the business by making accurate information easy to access. We curate and maintain high-quality data warehouses and pipelines that serve as the authoritative foundation for product and financial activity across Stripe, powering analytics, ML capabilities, agentic workflows, and merchant-facing data interfaces. Beyond building data, we act as the internal experts in data technologies and partner with Data Platform to deliver high-quality, low-friction data processing frameworks. We also serve as the bridge between data producers and data consumers — championing best-in-class data engineering practices and guiding product teams on event-driven data API modeling — so that every team at Stripe can build, decide, and grow from a trusted, well-engineered data foundation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a person who could contribute to the team by solving high-impact, cutting-edge data problems. The ideal candidate will be someone that has built data pipelines for large scale volume, is deeply knowledgeable of key tools including Airflow/Spark/Kafka/Flink, is empathetic, excels at building strong relationships, and collaborates effectively with other Stripe teams to understand their use cases and unlock new capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Lead the technical outcomes for a team of ambitious, talented engineers, providing mentorship, guidance, and support to ensure their success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with our recruiting team to attract and hire top talent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver cutting-edge data pipelines that scale to users&#39; needs, focusing on reliability and efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop strong subject matter expertise and manage the SLAs of data pipelines and full stack web applications that support critical stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product managers and peers across the company to create/improve canonical datasets and data warehouses, use golden paths, and ensure Stripes and customers are using trustworthy data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage AI/LLM and Agents at scale to produce and analyze high-quality data on ambiguous problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have the opportunity to drive the execution of key data initiatives for Stripe, overseeing the entire development lifecycle from planning to delivery while maintaining high standards of quality and timely completion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a collaborative and inclusive work environment, promoting innovation, knowledge sharing, and continuous improvement within the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a Staff-level role — that typically means 10+ years of experience building and operating data systems, pipelines, warehouses, infrastructure, and leading teams to deliver exceptional solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong engineering background and passion for data as well as prior experience with writing and debugging data pipelines using a distributed data framework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An inquisitive nature in diving into data inconsistencies to pinpoint issues, and resolve deep rooted data quality issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of a backend development language (such as Scala, Java, or Go) and strong SQL experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extreme customer focus, with a commitment to partnering with product, leaders across the business, and other Stripe engineers to understand their use cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective cross-functional collaboration, with the ability to think rigorously, communicate clearly, and make or coordinate difficult decisions and trade-offs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrive with high autonomy and responsibility in an ambiguous environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to foster and work in a healthy, inclusive, challenging, and supportive work environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our stack is made up of Iceberg, Kafka, Change Data Capture, Flink, Spark, Airflow, Hive Metastore, Pinot, Trino, and AWS Cloud - experience with all or some of these tools is a huge plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influencing open-source contributions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating and maintaining data marts / warehouses to power business reporting needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating with Product, Go-To-Market, or Sales / Marketing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine enjoyment of innovation and a deep interest in understanding how things work, with the ability to question and direct architectural decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills for various audiences, including leadership, users, and company-wide&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Service Infrastructure team is responsible for empowering teams to build highly reliable and performant services, backing our payment systems, fraud detection, and a multitude of other products. As an infrastructure team, you will build and expand the service frameworks to make complex systems easy to use, resilient, and scalable. We build powerful interfaces for engineers that depend on these systems—deployment, load balancers, web framework, databases, Kafka, and Kubernetes—while keeping them highly available and performant. We&#39;re looking for engineering leaders who drive the technical vision of Stripe&#39;s service infrastructure platform for thousands of engineers to use and build on top of, and thrive in a highly autonomous environment with many moving pieces.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join as a Technical Lead for one of the most impactful teams at Stripe. You will lead a team of engineers, collaborate with infrastructure and product engineering orgs, and advance service-oriented architecture (SOA) adoption at Stripe. By collaborating with the team&#39;s technical leaders, you will ensure the software your team builds meets the needs of Stripe and its customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a highly effective team that consistently delivers high-impact results while genuinely caring for one another. We expect you to bring your curiosity and critical thinking skills to this challenging domain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for individuals with a strong background in designing and delivering high-performance infrastructure products for both internal and external customers. We would love to hear from you whether you have spent your entire career in infrastructure or are looking to apply your skill set to the database engineering domain for the first time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a team of talented engineers, providing mentorship, guidance, and support to ensure their success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering Managers to create roadmaps that deliver milestones toward a cohesive engineering vision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand user needs and pain points to prioritize engineering work and deliver high-quality solutions that meet user needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the execution of projects, overseeing the entire development lifecycle from planning to delivery, while maintaining high standards of quality and timely completion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with high-visibility teams and their stakeholders to support the Infrastructure&#39;s key engineering initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Provide hands-on technical leadership (architecture and design, vision, direction, and requirements setting, and incident response processes) for team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with leaders across the company to create and drive toward the longer term vision of Stripe&#39;s services roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a collaborative and inclusive work environment, promoting innovation, knowledge sharing, and continuous improvement within the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of technical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in a strategic technical leadership role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading engineering team(s) working on API design, abstractions, frameworks, or client libraries (e.g., building internal or external developer products)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building infrastructure and products for internal or external customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of delivering pragmatic solutions that accelerate business growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to adjust conversations from high-level discussions to detailed coding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives on a high level of autonomy and responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear and persuasive writing and in-person communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills, critical thinking, determination, and a growth mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively with a diverse group of people, genuinely caring for each other and contributing to a high level of psychological safety for all team members and partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in at least one of the programming languages (Java, Ruby, Python, Go)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills for different audiences (leadership, users, company-wide)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a variety of common infrastructure platforms (databases, logging, event streams, metrics, caching, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading partially remote and distributed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing sustainable, in-house framework and abstraction ecosystems in large engineering orgs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building serverless platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing rigorous incident response processes and on-call rotations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We don&#39;t expect deep expertise in every dimension above, but genuine curiosity about any of the areas that are less familiar is important to us&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Startup Products team builds Stripe Atlas and other products that help founders start and run a company from anywhere in the world. We believe startups are one of the most effective ways to solve the world’s problems, and we want to give founders a running start—and keep them running.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We help founders form companies, raise capital, execute critical legal agreements, access the internet’s best tools, and automate their operations while feeling ambitious, smart, and assured. Our goal is to help more startups reach product-market fit, faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team comprises high-agency, high-ownership product thinkers who genuinely care about founders. Everyone is responsible for making our products the best they can be and ensuring our roadmap contains the highest-impact work for our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a broad and ambitious roadmap spanning global company formation, legal and financial workflows, AI-enabled operations, and products beyond Atlas. Delivering it requires strong technical leadership to shape future investments, de-risk complex initiatives, and build durable partnerships across Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Software Engineer on Startup Products, you will shape the technical strategy for the team while leading major 0→1 products from early exploration through launch and iteration. You will turn ambiguous opportunities into clear technical plans, align teams around those plans, and remain hands-on throughout execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work across product surfaces, services, APIs, data models, and integrations with internal and external systems. You will partner closely with Product, Design, Legal, Data, Operations, and engineering teams across Stripe to create experiences that make complex and consequential tasks feel simple and trustworthy for founders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and drive technical strategy across Startup Products, connecting near-term product delivery to a cohesive, durable engineering vision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead large, ambiguous 0→1 initiatives from problem definition and architecture through implementation, safe launch, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and maintain polished user experiences, reliable backend services, APIs, and systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify technical risks, dependencies, and foundational investments early, creating incremental plans that de-risk the roadmap and accelerate future work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering teams across Stripe, building alignment and influencing their roadmaps and priorities when Startup Products depends on shared capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with founders to understand their needs and translate complex legal, financial, and operational workflows into intuitive products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the team’s engineering bar through clear standards, strong documentation, mentoring, and constructive technical feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise product and engineering leadership on emerging opportunities, technical constraints, and investments needed to support the team’s long-term ambitions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of software engineering experience, with a track record of owning large, ambiguous systems end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience defining and delivering large, ambiguous software initiatives from early product and technical exploration through production launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong full-stack engineering skills, including experience building reliable backend services and polished user-facing product experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to create technical direction and align teams with different priorities and constraints without relying on direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product-minded engineering judgment, with a deep commitment to understanding users and delivering meaningful outcomes for them and the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication, with the ability to move between strategic discussions and detailed technical decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A high quality bar and attention to detail across product experience, implementation, reliability, and operational readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with early stage startups and a deep understanding of the challenges founders face all over the world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building 0→1 products and taking them from concept through launch and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building products involving legal, financial, compliance, or other complex and high-trust workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building AI-powered product experiences or platforms that safely automate consequential user tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Ruby, and/or TypeScript. We care more about strong engineering fundamentals and the ability to learn than expertise in a particular language or framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Storage Abstractions (STAX) team builds the software layer through which Stripe services access stored data. We own the database SDKs that hundreds of Ruby and Java services use to read and write data safely, reliably, and efficiently without needing to understand the underlying database, routing, or operational complexity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our work creates leverage across Stripe: by providing stable interfaces and safeguards at the storage layer, we help teams build products with confidence while enabling Stripe’s data architecture to evolve. Alongside engineers, we are designing for AI agents as customers of this foundation, making storage capabilities discoverable, interoperable, and safe to use across languages and storage backends.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Software Engineer on STAX, you will set technical direction and lead multi-year initiatives at the intersection of developer infrastructure, data access, and AI. You will work hands-on with engineers across Stripe to make storage access simpler, safer, and more interoperable, while helping product and infrastructure teams evolve their systems without fleet-wide migrations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will help turn Stripe’s AI strategy into practical developer infrastructure by treating AI agents as customers of the storage layer. This is an opportunity to build frameworks and interfaces that make complex storage operations discoverable, interoperable, and safe for both human developers and agentic workflows, while raising the quality bar for systems used throughout Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set technical direction for Stripe’s storage-access and lead high-impact initiatives from strategy through delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolve storage abstractions so service teams can use consistent and reliable capabilities across languages, API versions, and storage backends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design stable interfaces and guardrails that improve data correctness, reliability, observability, and performance by default&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treat AI agents as customers by building agent-accessible SDKs, frameworks, and developer workflows that enable safe, effective use of storage infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with senior leaders, engineers, product teams, and core infrastructure teams to solve cross-organizational data architecture challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers and raise the bar for technical design, execution, and operational excellence across the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a Staff-level role so we&#39;re looking for 12+ years of professional software engineering experience and&amp;nbsp;5+ years leading technical strategy and delivery for complex, cross-team engineering initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading engineering team(s) working on API design, SDKs, abstractions, frameworks, or client libraries (e.g., building internal or external developer products)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing reliable distributed systems with a focus on data correctness, performance, and safe evolution of critical infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work designing developer infrastructure for AI or agentic workflows and helping define a technical direction for their use&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated customer-centricity, with a track record of deeply understanding user needs and obsessing over delivering simple, reliable experiences for internal or external customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building infrastructure and products for internal or external customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of delivering pragmatic solutions that accelerate business growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to adjust conversations from high-level discussions to detailed coding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives on a high level of autonomy and responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear and persuasive writing and in-person communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills, critical thinking, determination, and a growth mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively with a diverse group of people, genuinely caring for each other and contributing to a high level of psychological safety for all team members and partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in at least one of the programming languages (Java, Ruby, Python)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with MongoDB or other large-scale storage systems, such as DynamoDB, Elasticsearch, RocksDB, or relational databases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience guiding adoption of a shared developer platform across a large internal engineering organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing observability and operational tooling that helps platform users diagnose and resolve issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in financial technology or another environment where data correctness and reliability are especially important&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience influencing product and organizational decisions with senior leaders and broad stakeholder groups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading partially remote and distributed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing rigorous incident response processes and on-call rotations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We don&#39;t expect deep expertise in every dimension above, but genuine curiosity about any of the areas that are less familiar is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe startups are the future. We work with many of the newest and most innovative companies to help them grow, and we need your help. We&#39;re looking for someone who knows their way around the early-stage startup ecosystem to represent Stripe and share what we&#39;re working on with a broad base of startups and accelerator partners. Our primary goal is to help early-stage founders succeed, and that comes in a variety of forms - mentorship, helping them set up their financial stack, connecting them with investors and mentors, being their internal advocate, and much more.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role you will oversee a portfolio of strategic early-stage accelerator partnerships, including Y Combinator, as we work to educate, attract and retain the most promising startups. You’re an energetic and organized self-starter; you understand the product well and can cultivate trusted partnerships with the right players in the ecosystem. You’re also able to succinctly communicate Stripe&#39;s mission and benefits to investors and startups. You will be on the front lines for evangelizing our product to prospective users and a key driver of our success with startups. You connect dots, constantly soliciting input from users and using that to improve product and GTM strategy. If you’re excited to spend your days interfacing with startup founders and early-stage investors, and find energy in tirelessly helping early-stage founders as they look to start and scale, then we’d love to talk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee our YC Combinator and other accelerator partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across the business to ensure that every founder&#39;s experience of Stripe is surprisingly delightful&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build out and oversee the execution of key programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spin up new initiatives that add continuous value to the Y Combinator ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a point of escalation for partners and top startups to grow Stripe’s brand within the Y Combinator ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a product feedback loop to internal teams to ensure that we continue to build for the highest potential businesses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross functionally with key internal stakeholders to advance strategic Stripe initiatives for startup founders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collate startup ecosystem insights and prepare weekly / quarterly updates detailing business progress, market trends, and product feedback gathered from startup engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Stripe in the startup ecosystem and take up speaking opportunities at key startup events that bolster Stripe as the best platform for founders to start and scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage your data prowess (SQL, etc) to build out tools that enable us to better serve founders and demonstrate impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest and demonstrated ability to cultivate deep, trust-based partnerships with some of the most consequential venture capitalists&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in the startup ecosystem with startup or investing experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced business or technical founder with a passion for helping other founders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the startup ecosystem, founder empathy, and ability to build strong partnerships, particularly within the Y Combinator community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A user-first mindset, anything less than perfect is unacceptable to you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work cross-functionally with internal and external stakeholders to get new programming off the ground.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re a builder by nature and are excited to launch new initiatives within Stripe that extend surprisingly delightful experiences to best in class founders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communications skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hunger and motivation to operate (and thrive) in a highly ambiguous and fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Humility, and who takes initiative with a “no task is too small” and “I’ll get it done” attitude.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Well-networked individual who is active in the early stage venture capital and startup ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Alumni of Y Combinator&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand a technical buyer and key moments in their life-cycle where financial infrastructure decisions are made.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adept public speaker, presenter and moderator.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sales experience, understands channel partnerships and the value this channel brings to a GTM org.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Data skills - conversant in SQL or Python - and willingness to build tools serve our users and measure business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Platform Sales team is a highly consultative, enterprise sales team that is responsible for some of Stripe’s largest and fastest growing partners. Stripe helps software platforms offer more value to their customers by embedding Stripe’s powerful payments technology into their solution. As a Platform Sales Manager, you will play a critical role on our go-to-market leadership bench-- leading a team of AEs to make payments-as-a-service a competitive advantage for high-growth organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive sales growth through successful leadership, organizational planning, customer service and outstanding execution&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the expansion of Stripe’s footprint with global saas platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make hiring decisions, honing our ideal candidate profile and onboarding strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create structure and focus for GTM ideas and product sales campaigns that the product team is exploring. Drive execution and measurement. Analyze results and make recommendations for action in a timely manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define key sales support mechanisms, processes, and programs to meet the rapid growth of the business and achieve revenue attainment and market development objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a world-class organization and write the playbook for the era of monetizing payments on platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a team of sophisticated Existing Business, Platform AEs focused on expanding our global footprint with enterprise SaaS platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive deal strategy and partner across the business to ensure healthy pipeline, funnel conversion, win rate, and margin preservation across the portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Stripe&#39;s product roadmap and drive best practices on selling and forecasting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with the largest strategic opportunities, leading executive relationships&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Being accountable for delivering revenue growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of relevant platform and/or payments sales experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of people management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to hire, coach, and motivate a high-performance sales team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to articulate complex, technical concepts and translate them into business-relevant terms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated quantitative and analytical skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives in fast-paced settings with a high-level of autonomy and can create clarity and structure&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A knack for working well with a wide range of stakeholders, both internally and externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience scoping and managing strategic projects with input from cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in financial services, the payments industry, or with the card networks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The AI GTM team is focused on one of Stripe&#39;s most strategic growth opportunities: enabling AI-native and AI-enabled businesses to scale on Stripe. We&#39;re in a unique position – partnering with the world&#39;s most ambitious AI companies (the likes of OpenAI, Anthropic, and NVIDIA) building on the frontier of artificial intelligence – across infrastructure, foundation models, agents, and applications – to grow globally with the help of Stripe&#39;s financial infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of Stripe&#39;s GTM organization, this team works closely with Product, Engineering, and Marketing to shape Stripe&#39;s AI GTM strategy and ensure that the world&#39;s leading AI companies – from early-stage innovators to the largest public players – choose to build with Stripe.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work collaboratively with one of Stripe’s most strategic customers to realize their business goals. Our customers in the AI Industry move fast, you’ll work alongside your customer to develop and execute a multi-year partnership strategy that accelerates their ambitions with Stripe as a critical partner.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role that will require you to be an active participant in Stripe’s product strategy across the company, acting as a proxy for your customer within the walls of Stripe. You will interact with executives internally and externally to ensure your customer’s needs are well understood and prioritized. You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own full commercial sales cycles and partnership opportunities, from business case development, to deal structuring and negotiating, to close&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a strategic account plan to expand Stripe’s commercial footprint within your customer’s business, driving growth through cross-sell, expansion, and new revenue streams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive deal strategy and commercial negotiations for large, complex renewals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop relationships with executive stakeholders within your customer’s business, deeply understanding problems they are trying to solve and helping them find durable solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be responsible for account mapping and coordinating meaningful conversations with the appropriate stakeholders, internally and externally, to expand the customer relationship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and contribute to team projects, further Stripe’s use of AI tools and agents, and help refine our sales processes and culture in Stripe’s GTM organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who operates with vision and urgency at the highest levels of enterprise sales. You combine deep commercial creativity with the executive presence to negotiate landmark agreements, and the strategic judgment to know which problems matter most. You thrive in ambiguity, create clarity for others, and have a track record of building and closing the largest, most complex deals in your organization&#39;s history.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success closing transformational partnerships with bespoke commercial structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;13+ years of sales experience selling technical products to large enterprises, with a sustained track record of top performance and quota overachievement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years leading complex sales cycles with Enterprise organizations required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of leading and orchestrating large cross-functional teams through complex deal cycles with competing priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build and maintain executive relationships at the C-suite level and influence strategic decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand complex technical architectures and craft creative solutions that span multiple products and commercial models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to develop and execute account plans spanning multiple business units across a complex organization and subsidiaries&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to command a room of senior executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate in a highly ambiguous and fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interest in technology and a deep understanding of the AI industry&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;History of shaping org-wide sales practices, mentoring peers, and contributing to team strategy beyond individual quota attainment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling into or partnering with frontier AI companies, hyperscalers, or developer-first platforms&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of AI monetization models (token-based pricing, usage-based billing, consumption entitlements, API rate structures)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a high-growth technology company where you helped define the go-to-market approach for a new or nascent market segment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Stripe&#39;s products and the broader fintech/payments ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Platform Sales team partners with Software Platforms to help them expand their value proposition towards payments and financial services by leveraging Stripe Connect. Platforms already using Stripe include Shopify, Treatwell, Sage &amp;amp; Wix.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of the Strategic Account Platforms team, you will manage and elevate our relationships with a limited number of our largest and most complex accounts. Your role is to identify and implement new growth opportunities and ways Stripe can exceed expectations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Strategic Account Executive, you will develop our partnerships with our largest and most complex Platforms by creating long term alignment between Stripe and your Platforms’ business strategy, technological roadmap and user experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for the relationship and business developed between Stripe and a limited number of Strategic Accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, document and implement strategies that are mutually beneficial to the Platforms you manage and Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, develop and orchestrate multi-level executives relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence and align multiple company leaders internally and externally, from engineering to marketing, from finance to compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full sales cycle from lead to close to activate for large enterprise-size deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to shaping our platform partnership strategy and building repeatable processes and scaled engagement models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are an adept salesperson and relationship manager capable of engaging in deep business-level and technical conversations at multiple levels of the organization, including the CTO, COO, CFO and CEO. You have experience working with large and complex accounts. You can lead complex, multi-party sales in a highly consultative manner. You are used to building value in competitive situations and enjoy working on products that require deep product understanding, combined with technical knowledge. You are naturally analytical and enjoy digging into business models and helping customers quantify their investment decisions. Finally, you enjoy building – you like to actively participate in the development of our sales process, the articulation of our value proposition, and the creation of key tools and assets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of sales experience, managing large accounts and selling complex technical solutions and closing large deals with a track record of top performance (if you do not have a sales background but have the grit and an experience of managing complex projects or consulting engagement, we are keen to hear from you)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of moving sales processes forward from inception to close by leading complex, multi-party sales in a highly consultative manner, understanding strategies and leading with value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great listening skills and ability to quickly become a trusted resource for C-levels decision-makers across technology and finance orgs within software companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ability to understand complex technical and business problems and understand how Stripe’s solutions can address them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A positive attitude and tireless work ethic when encountering blockers to success, whether external or internal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead complex negotiations involving bespoke commercial agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior verbal and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate in a highly ambiguous and fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interest in technology and a deep understanding of the space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in or excitement in learning about financial technology infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fastidious approach to CRM hygiene and experience utilizing thorough sales forecasting metrics on a weekly/quarterly basis and communicating them in a succinct manner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is building the economic engine for AI – and it’s working. Today, 88% of the Forbes AI 50 are building on Stripe (and most of the remaining 12% are pre-monetization).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The AI GTM team is focused on helping AI-native businesses monetize and scale. We&#39;re in a unique position—partnering with the world&#39;s most ambitious AI companies (like OpenAI, Anthropic, ElevenLabs, and NVIDIA) to help them grow. This is one of the fastest growing parts of the business, and we need more great people to help us continue to accelerate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Sales Manager on the AI GTM team at Stripe, you will leverage your sales leadership and product expertise to drive growth through new and existing strategic AI customers. Reporting to the Chief Revenue Officer of AI, you will lead a team of Account Executives responsible for expanding Stripe&#39;s relationship with some of the most important AI companies in the world—across payments, billing, and beyond.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be instrumental in leading in-depth product discussions with customers, developing consultative and solution-based sales strategies, and building deep knowledge of the AI industry and its unique monetization challenges. You will collaborate closely with Product, Marketing, Product Marketing, and User Operations teams to develop and execute against our go-to-market strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the long-term vision for a growing AI GTM team and scale day-to-day operations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and manage a team of Account Executives managing existing AI accounts (driving revenue expansion, product attach, and retention) and looking for new business opportunities. Establish strategic plans and objectives to drive growth across the AI GTM business line, guiding execution to KPIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and develop a high-performing team, fostering a strong culture of energized and engaged Stripes while investing in the growth and development of your team. Coach and guide the team in developing consultative and solution-based sales skills throughout the sales cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for driving revenue, increasing product attach rates, and growing existing clients at high rates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with Product, Marketing, and User Operations teams to influence our product roadmap (you are on the frontier!) and accelerate our growth trajectory for our AI industry users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as both an internal and customer-facing expert on Stripe&#39;s products, particularly as they apply to AI-native business models (usage-based billing, marketplace payments, embedded finance, agentic commerce).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong relationships with customer executives (CEO, CFO, CTO) and serve as a trusted advisor on how Stripe can support their growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create best practices and improve the business and customer engagement model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sales leader. You are an adept sales leader, capable of engaging in business-level and technical conversations at multiple levels of the organization. You see value in competitive situations and enjoy working on products that require both deep product understanding and technical knowledge, especially for AI industry users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;People developer. You are a strong people leader who builds high-performing teams through coaching, accountability, and culture. You&#39;re as comfortable working with clients as with internal stakeholders (including executives) and are excited to become an expert and share your knowledge. You possess an organized, self-starter mindset and excellent communication skills, with a track record for improving the processes and organizations around you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI enthusiast. You have deep context in the AI industry and are energized by keeping up with new developments in the space. You bring a user-first mindset— you approach every customer interaction as a consultative partner rather than a transactional seller.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Technically curious. You understand APIs, webhooks, and modern developer tools—and you can hold credible conversations with engineering leaders about how Stripe&#39;s infrastructure fits into their stack.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of sales leadership experience, launching and growing high-functioning sales teams/products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in hyper-growth SaaS or technology environments across the AMER region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success managing existing/growth customer portfolios and driving revenue expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to be a self-starter, capable of driving business results without significant supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand complex technical requirements and craft solutions across multiple stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of AI industry dynamics, business models, and monetization strategies (usage-based pricing, API-first distribution, agentic commerce).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product acumen—ability to learn and articulate complex product capabilities, understand how they work technically, and connect them to user needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills, including strong presentation skills for in-person meetings with multiple stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An enthusiastic &quot;roll up your sleeves&quot; mentality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead complex negotiations involving bespoke agreements with commercial and enterprise businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry experience in payments, financial infrastructure, developer tools, or AI/ML platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing relationships within the AI ecosystem (AI labs, AI-native SaaS companies, developer platforms).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling complex platform solutions involving multiple products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a growth-stage software company or a leading payments/fintech company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Stripe&#39;s product suite and how AI companies leverage financial infrastructure to scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is looking for a senior product strategist-operator to join the Strategic Business Performance (SBP) team. SBP is the&amp;nbsp;&quot;connective tissue&quot; of Stripe. You will have a front-row seat to how the company operates and a direct hand in ensuring we&amp;nbsp;hit our most important goals. If you are a technical strategist who loves to move fast and fix high-stakes problems, we’d love to hear from you.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SBP is a small, high-leverage group within Central Strategy &amp;amp; Operations at Stripe. Our mission is to create strategic&amp;nbsp;clarity around Stripe’s performance. We work with partner teams to report on the business; dive into it to support and&amp;nbsp;pressure-test our strategy, driving change wherever we find soft spots and enabling the success of other teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone who connects across data, financials and product &amp;amp; business strategy and can unearth a signal in the noise and either fix the problem directly or convene the right people to fix it fast.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will work cross-functionally within our group and across Stripe’s technical and user-facing teams to solve&amp;nbsp;problems and design workflows that benefit our users. Specifically:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the &quot;Signal&quot;&lt;/strong&gt;: You will define and maintain the metrics that actually matter for in-year performance. You’ll&amp;nbsp;develop a &quot;morning read&quot; discipline—a curated, high-signal view of the business that drives immediate action,&lt;br&gt;moving far beyond standard dashboarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep-Dive Interventions&lt;/strong&gt;: You will lead &quot;surge&quot; projects to diagnose and unblock critical goals at risk. You aren&#39;t just identifying problems; you are staying in the arena until the trajectory has measurably changed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bridge Product &amp;amp; Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;: You will translate long-horizon corporate theses into in-year operational reality. You’ll&amp;nbsp;take ambiguous opportunities that cut across product, risk, and marketing and decompose them into structured&lt;br&gt;workstreams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Synthesize for Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;: You’ll think ahead of our executive team, preparing CEO/COO-level materials that translate unstructured signals into structured diagnoses they can act on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pressure-test our Assumptions&lt;/strong&gt;: You’ll work closely with Corporate Strategy and Product teams to identify gaps&amp;nbsp;between our external market forces and our internal execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these&amp;nbsp;requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience in product/data analytics within product organizations or strategic business performance&amp;nbsp;teams at high-growth tech companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Product Strategy, Product Management, or GM-style roles where you owned a P&amp;amp;L or a specific&lt;br&gt;business outcome&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply curious about business models and data, probing into signals, understanding trends and customer usage patterns to uncover novel insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of directly driving business growth through analytical insights and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply AI to enhance decision-making and operational efficiency, know when and how to use the right AI tools to move faster without sacrificing rigor or quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product sense and the ability to understand the technical mechanics of how software products are built and scaled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience navigating ambiguous, cross-functional problems and leading high-stakes interventions with senior stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience with fintech products or complex financial systems is a plus, but not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience facilitating senior leadership/ stakeholder meetings to drive meaningful conversations regarding&amp;nbsp;Stripe’s business performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Payments ecosystem, or experience in finance or fintech is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build trust and partner with senior leaders and CXOs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical proficiency in SQL / Python / R and data analysis; ability to self-serve and perform independent deep-dives into complex datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving creative solutions with and effectively informing the roadmap of cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand the implications of Stripe ships such as product features, policy changes, and marketing&amp;nbsp;outreach on the user experience and resulting support experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is building tools to help our users create and scale their businesses, and grow the GDP of the internet. The Workforce Management team at Stripe helps manage our growing support operations network of both internal and external resources by consulting on operational change initiatives, modeling support requirements, and managing workload and resource allocations for an optimal user experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Strategic Capacity Planning Specialist, you will play a key role in designing and maintaining capacity planning models for one of our key user support or risk verticals, with a focus on user experience, budget, utilization, and speed of answer to our users&#39; queries. You will operate in a fast-paced and energizing environment surrounded by top talent, where resilience and openness to feedback will be key to success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Develop and maintain capacity planning models to forecast resource requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage forecasting techniques to analyze historical data and market trends, predicting future capacity needs and enabling informed planning decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate potential risks and opportunities regarding model inputs to inform planning decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor performance against planned capacity levels and adjust plans as needed, while holding stakeholders accountable for the accuracy of plan inputs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the vendor delivery team and stakeholders to gather information and align planning efforts with Stripe&#39;s business goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate data from multiple SQL databases to automate reporting processes and streamline data collection for capacity planning and forecasting purposes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate planning results and recommendations to senior leadership and stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a strategic partner in our intake process, providing subject-matter expertise for any requests affecting resourcing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze production or service delivery data to determine utilization rates and identify areas for improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Bachelor&#39;s degree in Statistics, Mathematics, Data Analytics, Computer Science, Business, or Economics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in capacity planning for medium to large organizations, as well as workforce management for internal and outsourced workforces (BPO)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong SQL skills, with experience in data integration and automation for process optimization, alongside knowledge of Tableau or comparable tools to perform data analysis independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and presentation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of outsourcing practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Financial/budgeting background&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of WFM tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Alliances and Channels team owns the Go-To-Market (GTM) partnerships for Stripe including management consultants, payment advisors, systems integrators and technology partners.&amp;nbsp; We drive the development of the partnerships including enablement and solution design along with the go-to-market strategy where we work with partners to source new opportunities for Stripe and ensure they are delivered and activated with world class quality.&amp;nbsp; Additionally, we work to ensure our partners develop large, fast growing, profitable businesses on Stripe inclusive of payments, billing, fraud, stablecoins and agentic offerings.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the lead for Stripe relationship with Strategic payment advisors you will drive Stripe’s engagement with payment advisors who most critically influence opportunities relevant to Stripe. Payment advisors firms help large and medium businesses with all their needs related to payment, including monetizing payments through marketplaces and platforms, RFP execution, GTM, Cost optimization, new revenue modes and GTM strategies. Often an enterprises’ financial infrastructure is the cornerstone of these transformations and legacy players are being challenged on their innovation ability in a crowded and rapidly evolving space. Therefore, Stripe needs to continuously engage, educate and support this broad base of influencers to ensure they clearly understand the value and capabilities that Stripe brings to these initiatives, early in the process. Ensuring that Stripe is included in the right consideration sets and that these partners have access to resources in Stripe in service of their users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The lead lead will work to engage firms directly and via scaled mechanisms partnering with product, marketing and GTM teams. The covered firms will be the like of Glenbrook, CMSPI, EDG, with the goal of developing of a purpose built program to support these firms and ensure they have fast access to the relevant information and expert ultimately leading to Stripe being a preferred/short listed provider of commerce transformations and platform use cases being recommended by these firms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and build a scalable program to engage these firms individually and broadly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage firms to create thought leadership exchange and deep awareness of Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define Metrics for success, iterating overtime as we learn what works.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategically engage internal subject matter experts and resources to timely support partners requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define incentives program specific for payment advisors that accounts for their role as agnostic advisors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with Stripe marketing, analyst and industry leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and evolve this new role for the A&amp;amp;C organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present innovative payments solutions to partners and their clients including stablecoins and agentic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organize and execute Periodical Business Reviews with each partner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure business development targets are met through these partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure Stripe is brought in the consideration set for relevant RFPs and opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8-12 years of experience in payments or operations at a leading technology company, or consultancy in the payments industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience working for or with payment advisory firms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience leading complex payment and related projects including implementation and optimisation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to build collaborative working relationships with cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to deal effectively with ambiguity and thrive in an unstructured, fast-moving environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to be a self-starter capable of driving business results without significant supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to identify and pursue commercial opportunities through partners by structuring mutually beneficial outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent presentation skills and demonstrated public speaking experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous/current use of Stripe products.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry experience in Retail, Hospitality, Insurance, Media, Healthcare.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Management experience, leading global teams (direct and indirect).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Procurement is part of Stripe Finance and owns the full supplier lifecycle and buying journey. The team sources and evaluates new vendors, renews and negotiates contracts with existing suppliers, and leads third‑party risk management and compliance activities to ensure suppliers meet Stripe’s standards. Procurement also drafts, reviews, and approves supplier contract structures and terms, aligned with Stripe’s risk appetite and legal requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an experienced Sourcing professional to focus on establishing trusted business partner relationships in the technology space at Stripe with a “users first” approach to ensure early and active participation across the full lifecycle of strategic sourcing and procurement, including: category planning, sourcing strategies, RFx execution, supplier evaluation and selection, contract negotiations and management, and continuous improvements. You will play a critical role in ensuring Stripe&#39;s procurement aligns with our operational principles by contributing to our sustainable growth while fostering strong, ethical supplier relationships. Experience with complex software negotiations is required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute strategic sourcing plans for designated categories, identifying opportunities for cost reduction, quality improvement, and process efficiencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead supplier selection, assessment, and contract negotiation processes, ensuring compliance with Stripe&#39;s policies and risk management protocols&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct market research and analysis to inform category strategies and stay ahead of industry trends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be an active champion across the company supporting our third party risk programs and fiscal initiatives when engaging in Procurement activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver on strategic sourcing management goals including cost savings and spend under management, and implement any necessary process enhancements to ensure that those goals are achieved&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate existing supplier base and identify rationalization and/or RFx opportunities in partnership with business teams and Finance, allowing Stripe to maximize negotiating leverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with internal teams to drive enterprise-level procurement solutions and increase supplier management effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in establishing short-term and long range planning and budget development of the company to support strategic business goals&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help to develop and execute a roadmap to build and scale an impactful Strategic Sourcing &amp;amp; Category Management function that Stripes recognize and value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of 8 years of experience in indirect sourcing, procurement, category management, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to develop and implement strategic sourcing and category management strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven negotiation skills and a track record of achieving significant cost savings and supplier value without compromising on quality or service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to manage and interpret complex data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in supplier contracting with a solid understanding of standard commercial terms and conditions to mitigate risks and create clear service level agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leadership and stakeholder management skills with the ability to elevate ambitions and influence cross-functional and internal team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solution-oriented mindset with enthusiasm for establishing best practice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-disciplined, diligent, proactive and detail oriented&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with a rapid pace of change, complexity, and working across matrixed functions, preferably within a fast-paced technology or financial services environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic mindset with the ability to make sound business decisions based on data and analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding or experience with e-procurement tools and systems (e.g., Zip, Workday Strategic Sourcing, Oracle, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the fintech industry and its supply chain and procurement challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Payments Performance (GPPT) team, which falls under the Customer Success organization, is a dedicated team of payment experts that help users optimize their payment and product setup with Stripe. The team provides direct User engagement to our most strategic Users as well as a variety of resources that support account teams (self-guided payment optimization workshops, optimization playbooks, data &amp;amp; insights).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Customer Success Strategy &amp;amp; Operations team sits at the center of how Customer Success operates at Stripe. As GPPT scales, dedicated S&amp;amp;O support is required to both shape the function’s day-to-day operating model—from operating forums, capacity management and metric design— to the systems and cadences that enable execution of the team&#39;s long term vision. You will lead annual planning, OKR development, and engagement-model design to ensure GPPT is positioned to deliver for users and scale effectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact Business Partner and Builder role at the heart of GPPT and Customer Success. As a trusted thought partner to senior leadership, you’ll combine strategic insight, operational excellence, and hands-on execution to turn ambitious priorities into meaningful results. You’ll lead critical cross-functional initiatives and build the operating mechanisms that help teams make smarter decisions, execute with consistency, scale effectively, and deliver measurable value. Given the cross functional nature of our S&amp;amp;O org and the connective tissue we serve amongst post sales teams, you will also be responsible for leading a number of critical programs such as our global churn initiative.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you enjoy moving between strategic problem-solving and hands-on execution—and bring a roll-up-your-sleeves mindset—this role is for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The near-term focus of this role is to build the operational foundations of the GPPT business from the ground up. This includes building operating models, processes, business cadences, systems, team capacity management and reporting infrastructure to support a growing and increasingly specialised organization. As a key business partner, you’ll measure and analyse performance, develop metrics and dashboards, and lead data-informed process improvements that help the GPPT team operate more efficiently and deliver greater customer impact. You will also be responsible for running a number of cross functional projects such as our global Churn program that require dedicated oversight.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and run the GPPT operating model which will include including process, governance, forums, capacity modelling and metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop reports and dashboards to meet key reporting requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement AI-enabled workflows that improve GPPT efficiency, scalability, and customer impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhance business processes through data-driven decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and monitor annual and quarterly OKRs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare materials for QBRs and other leadership meetings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct analysis and investigation of system operations and workflow management. Work cross-functionally to analyze and troubleshoot system challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Running cross functional &amp;amp; high impact global programs such as Churn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of work experience, with a significant portion in strategic / operational roles at high-growth tech companies or consulting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High comfort with ambiguity (and context switching) —you take an undefined operational problem, scope it, design a solution, and drive it to completion with minimal oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience holding a high bar across operational design, strategic planning, and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable working independently with minimal oversight while holding yourself accountable to deadlines.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience building operational foundations from the ground up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have project/program management experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working cross functionally with senior stakeholders. You&#39;re comfortable bringing an independent and opinionated perspective.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical proficiency in AI tools in order to automate workflows as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical rigor—you&#39;re comfortable owning data and metrics directly, running your own analyses, and pressure-testing assumptions without relying on a dedicated analytics partner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage technical resources and translate business needs into requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with Go-to-Market teams including Customer Success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Payments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deal Pricing is a dedicated global function that provides deal pricing expertise, financial insights, and deal support for negotiated users to Stripe&#39;s global Go-to-Market teams. We work to ensure deals create economic value for Stripe by establishing the deal commercial framework for a scaling sales organization, actively supporting large and strategic deals, and providing pricing insights and feedback to sales, finance, and product leaders. Deal Pricing frequently works with cross-functional business partners across Operations, Finance and Strategy, and Product. There is constant collaboration with Deal Pricing colleagues across all regions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rather than pricing individual deals, this &lt;strong&gt;Strategy and Operations (S&amp;amp;O)&lt;/strong&gt; role acts as a central engine &lt;em&gt;behind&lt;/em&gt; the global deal pricing team. You’ll serve as a &quot;Chief of Staff&quot; function to Deal Pricing leadership—owning the global operating model, driving cross-functional process excellence, managing our strategic operating rhythm, and codifying our commercial knowledge so Stripe can scale its GTM velocity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic planning and operating rhythm&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive strategy execution.&lt;/strong&gt; Translate high-level annual goals into actionable quarterly OKRs, ensuring clear ownership and measurable progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage the operating cadence.&lt;/strong&gt; Facilitate the team’s operating rhythm (MBRs, QBRs, and leadership syncs) to drive accountability, surface risks, and unblock cross-functional dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic telemetry and insights.&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate with our tooling and analytics team to track functional performance, using data to inform pricing strategy, operational pivots, and executive decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial governance and friction management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optimize cross-functional SLAs.&lt;/strong&gt; Act as the primary bridge between Sales velocity and risk-mitigation functions (Deal Strategy, Finance, Treasury). Define and enforce SLAs for deal pricing approvals to ensure global consistency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resolve bottlenecks.&lt;/strong&gt; Proactively identify process friction, working with partner ops teams to redesign playbooks and clarify decision-making boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge infrastructure and sales enablement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Codify the &quot;Deal pricing playbook.&quot;&lt;/strong&gt; Build and maintain a single source of truth for deal pricing frameworks, guidelines, and Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs), ensuring documentation is version-controlled and highly discoverable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scale sales self-service.&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Sales Enablement to translate complex commercial policies into self-serve guides and playbooks, empowering Sales to execute simple deals independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process and AI architecture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems roadmap.&lt;/strong&gt; Act as a lead for our CRM and CPQ evolution, transforming manual, spreadsheet-based pricing into automated, scalable workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deploy AI for efficiency.&lt;/strong&gt; Proactively identify and implement AI and LLM solutions to accelerate operations—including automating documentation, summarizing legacy contract terms, and extracting data from unstructured sales communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Operations Management, Finance, Economics, Management, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6–8+ years of experience in Business Operations (BizOps), Sales and Revenue Operations, Management Consulting, or a Chief of Staff role supporting a high-growth GTM team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience using generative AI tools (e.g., LLMs, advanced prompting techniques, AI-driven search/synthesis tools) to accelerate your work. While not a software engineer, you are “technically savvy.” You can navigate data structures and AI orchestration tools to build prototypes or initial solutions independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience translating high-level corporate strategy into operational execution frameworks (OKRs, KPIs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding written communication skills. You must be able to write clear, structured, and highly professional playbooks and memos (critical for Stripe’s document-centric culture).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of mapping complex, cross-functional processes, identifying root causes of friction, and redesigning workflows to improve cycle times.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of GTM tech stacks (Salesforce, CPQ, workflow automation) and how to write clear business requirement documents (BRDs) for technical teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Fintech, Payments, or consumption-based (API) SaaS models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience building simple automation flows to optimize personal or team productivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Strategy &amp;amp; Operations (S&amp;amp;O) team for Infra is responsible for enabling the continued rapid growth and operational excellence of one of Stripe&#39;s most strategic areas - the infrastructure group. This role sits at the intersection of product, engineering, strategy, finance, data, GTM and day-to-day execution, ensuring the infra organization is well-informed, running efficiently and poised to deliver on the future product needs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a key member of this team, you will tackle a diverse array of challenges that underpin Stripe’s technical foundations which will span system scalability, platform reliability, and efficiency. You will provide the analytical rigor and operational pragmatism necessary to scale &lt;strong&gt;Stripe’s infrastructure&lt;/strong&gt; in a way that is both technically resilient and fiscally sustainable. Operating with a high degree of autonomy, you will lead critical strategic projects, translate complex system performance and capacity trends into actionable infrastructure requirements, and drive the high-stakes architectural and resource decisions necessary for Stripe’s long-term growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Infrastructure Strategy &amp;amp; Operations team is a vital partner to Stripe’s engineering leadership and the Office of the CPTO, focused on three core pillars:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Setting and Driving the Engineering Agenda:&lt;/strong&gt; We design the organizational structures and operating models that enable our infrastructure to scale ahead of the business. We lead critical technical governance forums and synthesize system-level health metrics such as &lt;strong&gt;utilization, latency, and fleet reliability&lt;/strong&gt; into strategic insights for senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Capacity &amp;amp; Infrastructure Planning:&lt;/strong&gt; We deliver objective, data-driven strategies for our platform roadmap. By modeling &lt;strong&gt;future infrastructure needs&lt;/strong&gt; against business growth forecasts, we ensure our global hardware and software investments are proactive rather than reactive, bridging the gap between deep engineering requirements and financial reality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program/Process Incubation:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; We add structure and clarity to ambiguous problems, leading and influencing large cross-functional teams to stand up and define new programs and processes that simplify how we run the business. We lead cross-functional initiatives to stand up new programs focused on infrastructure efficiency and resource optimization without compromising developer velocity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Infrastructure leadership to define the long-term strategic vision and build the annual operating plans, ensuring alignment with Stripe&#39;s overall company strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a pulse on the financial health/cost of Infrastructure including relevant trends, and proactively surface areas of concern or opportunity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and own models for in-depth analyses &amp;amp; benchmark key metrics to help inform our overall strategy and make the right growth decisions for Infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Obsess over our top infrastructure efficiency metrics, helping to surface, track, and drive initiatives that will move the needle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support cross-functional execution across priority projects, ensuring alignment between teams (e.g., product, engineering, marketing, sales, support).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement operational systems and processes (e.g., reporting dashboards, planning forums, decision-making workflows) that help the infrastructure group scale efficiently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience in strategy &amp;amp; operations, data science, finance, product management, or similar roles at technology companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in highly cross functional settings, and in a role that spans strategy, analysis, and operations in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Critical and first principles thinking (e.g., ability to question how we are working rather than simply executing), and the ability to zoom out to the most important questions &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for digging deep into data and problem solving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in data analytics with demonstrated ability in navigating large data sets and/or SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication with the the ability to speak to leaders across different teams, such as partnerships, product, engineering, and sales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to thrive in influence without authority environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good balance of business and technical acumen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ability to execute with minimal guidance, and in contexts with a high degree of ambiguity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in Infrastructure strategy (e.g., Compute, Storage, Networking, IT, Security or Developer Platforms), the Payments ecosystem, or high-scale Fintech is highly preferred.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to facilitate large-scale technical forums and planning sessions, maintaining a&amp;nbsp; focus on measurable goals, infrastructure SLAs, and ROI-driven outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving creative solutions for capacity and efficiency bottlenecks, with a track record of effectively influencing the roadmaps of cross-functional engineering and product teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is looking for a senior product strategist-operator to support the Risk team. Risk is central to Stripe’s ability to grow safely: the team protects Stripe and our users while enabling durable, responsible growth. In this role, you will have a front-row seat to high-stakes business and product decisions and a direct hand in helping the team identify emerging risks, prioritize the right interventions, and deliver measurable outcomes. If you are a technical strategist who moves quickly, brings clarity to ambiguity, and stays with difficult problems through resolution, we’d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will partner closely with Risk leaders and cross-functional teams across Product, Engineering, Data Science, Finance, Operations, and Strategy. You will create strategic clarity around Risk’s performance, connect business and product signals, pressure-test plans, and mobilize teams when results are off track. The role combines rigorous analysis with hands-on execution: you will not only identify where Stripe should act, but also help drive the work required to change the trajectory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone who can connect risk signals, data, financial performance, user impact, and product and business strategy. You can find the signal in the noise, form a clear point of view, and either address the problem directly or convene the right people to solve it quickly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will work across Risk and Stripe’s technical and user-facing teams to improve decision-making, strengthen execution, and help Stripe manage risk while serving users well.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the signal: Define and maintain the metrics that matter for Risk’s in-year performance, spanning risk outcomes, business impact, operational health, and user experience. Build a disciplined “morning read”—a curated, high-signal view that surfaces emerging issues and drives timely action beyond standard dashboarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead deep-dive interventions: Run focused “surge” efforts to diagnose and unblock critical goals at risk. Move from symptom to root cause, align teams on the response, and stay engaged until the trajectory has measurably improved.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bridge Risk, Product, and Strategy: Translate long-horizon company and risk theses into in-year priorities and operating plans. Decompose ambiguous opportunities and threats that cut across Product, Risk, Operations, and go-to-market teams into structured workstreams with clear owners and outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize for leadership: Anticipate the questions senior leaders will ask and prepare clear, decision-oriented materials that turn complex and unstructured risk signals into diagnoses, options, and recommended actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pressure-test assumptions: Work closely with Risk, Corporate Strategy, Product, and Finance to test whether plans reflect external market dynamics, changing risk patterns, user needs, and Stripe’s execution capacity. Identify gaps early and help teams adapt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience in product strategy, business operations, data analytics, product management, or strategic business performance roles, ideally in high-growth technology companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in product strategy, product management, or GM-style roles with direct ownership of a P&amp;amp;L or a specific business outcome&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply curious about business models and data, probing into signals, understanding trends and customer usage patterns to uncover novel insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of directly driving business growth through analytical insights and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to apply AI to improve decision-making and operational efficiency, with sound judgment about when and how to use AI tools without sacrificing rigor or quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product sense and the ability to understand the technical mechanics of how software products are built and scaled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience navigating ambiguous, cross-functional problems and leading high-stakes interventions with senior stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience with fintech products or complex financial systems is a plus, but not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience facilitating senior leadership and stakeholder discussions that lead to clear decisions and action on business performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in risk, payments, financial services, or fintech&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build trust and partner with senior leaders and CXOs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical proficiency in SQL / Python / R and data analysis; ability to self-serve and perform independent deep-dives into complex datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing creative solutions and influencing the roadmaps of cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to anticipate how product launches, policy changes, and go-to-market activity affect risk outcomes, user experience, and support operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;One of the company&#39;s most important strategic priorities is to build great products and experiences for Enterprises—and we are at an inflection point in the growth of our Enterprise business, with significant momentum.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Enterprise team is responsible for ensuring all of Stripe&#39;s products and services best fit the unique needs of global, modernizing enterprises. Our Enterprise Product extends beyond our APIs and dashboards—to Enterprise executive engagement, our perception in the market, our partner ecosystem, how we collaborate with our users to bring them live, and our users&#39; day-to-day interactions with our GTM and support teams—they&#39;re all part of the Product experience for these users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We focus on expanding and innovating on Stripe&#39;s platform in ways that help the largest and most complex customers run their businesses. Our work is highly cross-functional—partnering with almost every other team at Stripe—to execute on the priorities that matter most to Enterprises and ensure that they are successful on Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of the Enterprise Strategy and Operations team, you&#39;ll build the infrastructure, processes, and organizational muscle to help our Enterprise business scale:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-cutting company strategy projects and collaborate with teams to implement changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with multiple stakeholders across Enterprise and other Stripe teams (e.g., product teams, marketing, sales, support) to achieve the goals of the Enterprise Engine Catalyst. You&#39;ll need to objectively evaluate teams&#39; competing priorities and align stakeholders on the optimal solution for Stripe and our users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with senior leaders and cross-functional teams to accelerate progress, develop new operating models, and incubate new programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish new operating models in collaboration with key cross-functional teams, focusing on roadmap development and context alignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate annual and long-range planning efforts across teams contributing to the Enterprise segment, and drive alignment with partner teams to ensure a cohesive approach to planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive projects, timelines, and commitments on internal projects and customer deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in strategy and operations, product strategy, product management, or similar roles at technology companies, including highly cross-functional work spanning strategy, product, analysis, and operations in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Critical thinking and first-principles thinking (e.g., ability to question how we work rather than simply executing), and the ability to zoom out to the most important questions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong program management skills with experience managing end-to-end execution of projects and programs that have transformed their company&#39;s operations and delivered quantifiable business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication with the ability to speak to leaders across different teams, such as partnerships, product, engineering, and sales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to thrive in influence without authority environments, execute with minimal guidance, and operate in contexts with a high degree of ambiguity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Payments ecosystem or Enterprise software experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build trust and partner with senior leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to extract the key themes and learnings from a program and build business and investment cases based on these insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with SQL or constructing dashboards and structuring advanced data analysis to measure program success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand the implications of Stripe ships such as product features, policy changes, and marketing outreach on the user experience and resulting support experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet. We have a significant amount of work ahead, which gives you the opportunity to help put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;about-the-strategy-and-transformation-team&quot;&gt;About the Strategy and Transformation team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Strategy and Transformation team helps Stripe’s largest and most strategic users define and execute high-impact business and technology transformations. We work early in the customer lifecycle, alongside account teams and senior customer leaders, to connect business ambition with a practical path to value on Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team has established foundational Strategy and Transformation Consultant coverage across regions. We are now adding specialist advisors with differentiated expertise for enterprise conversations where Stripe’s role must be understood not simply as a payments provider, but as an integrated financial backbone within a customer’s broader commerce and technology ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;about-the-role&quot;&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Strategy and Transformation Advisor, Enterprise Commerce Architecture, you will be the senior strategic advisor for complex enterprise commerce pursuits in AMER. You will help customers develop a clear, prescriptive point of view on how Stripe should fit within their future-state architecture and what that means for their commerce platforms, order management systems, enterprise resource planning (ERP) and finance estate, customer and loyalty systems, identity, data platforms, fulfillment operations, and engineering organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a pre-sales role within the Strategy and Transformation Practice. You will partner with Go-to-Market (GTM), Solutions Architecture, Product, and Professional Services to increase customer confidence in Stripe’s ability to support consequential enterprise transformations. You will engage senior technical and business stakeholders, including chief technology officers, chief information officers, chief architects, vice presidents of engineering, and digital or commerce leaders. You will translate their strategic priorities into an enterprise commerce architecture, sequenced transformation roadmap, and clear implementation principles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will define the strategic architectural “what” and “why,” including the target state, key design principles, trade-offs, dependencies, and path to value. You will also provide technical advisory support to Stripe’s Integration Engineers, Solutions Architects, and Strategy and Transformation Consultants on the most complex opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-you-will-do&quot;&gt;What you will do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;shape-enterprise-commerce-transformation-strategy&quot;&gt;Shape enterprise commerce transformation strategy&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead executive discovery, strategy, and architecture workshops for Stripe’s most strategic enterprise prospects and users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess a customer’s current commerce and technology landscape. Identify how payments and financial infrastructure interact with commerce, order management, ERP and finance, customer relationship management (CRM), loyalty, identity, data, fulfillment, and risk systems. Develop a prescriptive future-state point of view for how Stripe can serve as a financial backbone within that architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate business objectives, such as international expansion, omnichannel commerce, marketplace growth, subscription transformation, cost optimization, improved authorization performance, and faster product development, into clear architecture and operating model implications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the enterprise-level principles, system boundaries, ownership models, integration patterns, data flows, and migration considerations needed to support the target state.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create multi-phase, dependency-aware transformation roadmaps that connect Stripe capabilities to measurable business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;increase-confidence-in-strategic-enterprise-pursuits&quot;&gt;Increase confidence in strategic enterprise pursuits&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with account teams, enterprise service managers, sales leaders, and senior solutions architects to identify pursuits where enterprise commerce architecture expertise will materially improve customer confidence or decision quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage credibly with executive technical stakeholders as a strategic advisor and peer, rather than as a product vendor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help customers understand the practical trade-offs between their current architecture and a future state that uses Stripe more deeply.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create clear executive narratives, architecture artifacts, transformation roadmaps, and decision materials that make Stripe’s role in the customer’s future state concrete.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support account strategy, opportunity shaping, and value articulation for complex, multi-product enterprise pursuits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help define the path from an initial architecture vision to implementation scope, while ensuring detailed solution design and delivery ownership remain with the appropriate Stripe teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;advise-and-support-stripes-and-our-users-technical-teams&quot;&gt;Advise and support Stripe’s and our users’ technical teams&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a senior thought partner to Integration Engineers, Solutions Architects, Account Executives, and Strategy and Transformation Consultants on complex enterprise architecture questions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide guidance on how to frame Stripe’s capabilities within broader enterprise commerce, finance, and data architectures across industries and segments, including insurance, fintech, retail, media and entertainment, marketplaces, and platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help user teams work through architecture-level issues, including system-of-record boundaries, application programming interface (API) and event design, data ownership, reconciliation, operational resilience, migration strategy, and organizational readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach internal teams on executive technical storytelling, architecture discovery, and translating technical decisions into business value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build reusable enterprise commerce architecture frameworks, reference patterns, workshop methods, and transformation narratives that improve the team’s effectiveness across AMER.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;inform-stripes-enterprise-strategy-and-product-direction&quot;&gt;Inform Stripe’s enterprise strategy and product direction&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring recurring customer architecture patterns, friction points, and unmet needs to Product, Engineering, and GTM leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify emerging enterprise commerce trends, including artificial intelligence (AI)-enabled commerce and financial operations, omnichannel experiences, embedded finance, platform business models, and global expansion. Translate these trends into relevant Stripe points of view.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to Stripe’s differentiated perspective on enterprise commerce transformation through internal thought leadership and selective customer-facing content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;minimum-qualifications&quot;&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience in enterprise architecture, technology strategy, digital transformation, management consulting, or senior technical advisory roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience advising large enterprises on complex technology transformation, ideally spanning commerce, payments, financial systems, or customer-facing platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to engage credibly with C-suite and vice president-level business and technical leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of enterprise commerce architecture, including systems such as commerce platforms, order management, ERP and finance, CRM, loyalty, identity, fulfillment, and cloud data platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of API-first integration, distributed systems, event-driven architecture, cloud platforms, data flows, and enterprise operational models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of payments and financial infrastructure, including acceptance, acquiring, settlement, reconciliation, fraud and risk, compliance, and multi-party payment models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to connect architecture decisions to business outcomes, including revenue growth, conversion, authorization performance, operational efficiency, resilience, cost, and speed to market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written, verbal, and visual communication skills, including the ability to make complex architecture decisions understandable to executive audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading ambiguous, cross-functional strategic engagements from initial discovery through a practical recommendation and roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Stripe or comparable payments and financial infrastructure platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in enterprise retail, marketplaces, platforms, software as a service (SaaS), travel, media, mobility, or other complex commerce environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience across omnichannel commerce, global payment methods, subscriptions, business-to-business payments, marketplaces, embedded finance, or platform monetization models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with enterprise architecture frameworks and methods, such as capability modeling, value stream analysis, domain-driven design, and transformation roadmapping.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising on data architecture, reconciliation, risk and fraud operations, AI-enabled financial operations, or commerce personalization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of coaching senior technical practitioners and influencing cross-functional teams without direct reporting authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;External credibility through senior customer advisory work, industry speaking, publications, or contributions to enterprise technology or payments communities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Privy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to make privacy and user ownership the default online. To do so, we build simple, flexible APIs and tools for developers that make it easy to build new products on crypto rails.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Privy owns the abstractions and infrastructure layer above wallets, integrating across chains, third-party providers, and Stripe products like Treasury and Link. We get to solve hard technical problems while leveraging Stripe&#39;s distribution to reach customers like Ramp, Klarna, Deel, Kraken, Hyperliquid, and Fomo — powering experiences for both mainstream users and crypto natives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learn more about Privy:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://privy.io/blog/announcing-our-acquisition-by-stripe&quot;&gt;Privy and Stripe: Bringing crypto to everyone&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Support Operations Associate at Privy, you will own the internal systems and workflows that keep our Developer Success team efficient, responsive, and focused. You’ll serve as air traffic control for support requests – triaging issues across our support stack (Pylon, Slack, HubSpot, and more), improving internal workflows, and maintaining CRM and support-data hygiene.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll partner closely with Account Management, Solutions Engineers, Forward Deployed Engineers, and Sales, while your day-to-day work will have impact across Privy, and Stripe as a whole.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-leverage operations role where attention to detail, a systems mindset, and a bias for execution will make you critical to making our customers successful.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own triage and routing for inbound support tickets from both Privy developers and end users of Privy applications, ensuring issues are assigned, tracked, and resolved promptly and efficiently across the Developer Success team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain data hygiene, consistency, and accuracy across our support stack, including Pylon, Slack, HubSpot, and other systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with cross-functional teams—including Sales, Engineering, and Product—to continuously improve the quality and efficiency of support processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain internal runbooks for ticket triage, escalations, and engineering-support handoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify operational gaps and implement scalable workflows that help the team respond to customers more effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1–3 years of experience in support operations, customer experience, technical program management, or a related operational role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized and process-driven, with strong attention to detail and a bias toward action and ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong intuition for customer sentiment and urgency, with sound judgment about how to prioritize and escalate issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with customer-support tooling, such as Pylon, Zendesk, Intercom, or Jira, and communication platforms like Slack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working across systems and maintaining high-quality CRM data in tools such as HubSpot or Salesforce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, especially for issue tracking, coordination, and process documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A systems mindset and enthusiasm for building internal processes that scale with the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a developer-tools or infrastructure company, or experience working closely with engineering and product teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with APIs, coding with AI, or using AI to automate tasks and operational processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

