&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community You Will Join&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Online Data organization helps Airbnb&#39;s builders create real-time data experiences through intuitive data interfaces and tools, with no database expertise required. Within Online Data, the Transactional Storage Services team owns the core storage infrastructure behind Airbnb&#39;s online data systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We design, build, and operate a new source-of-truth, horizontally scalable, open-source NewSQL database running on stateful Kubernetes. It holds Airbnb&#39;s critical user, listing, and financial data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join the Database Kernel team, which owns performance, reliability, and stability for Airbnb&#39;s NewSQL engine at scale. The team&#39;s work centers on the storage layer and query execution engine, and also covers consensus and shard management. In this role you&#39;ll dig into database internals to diagnose and fix SQL latency and availability issues. You&#39;ll also work closely with our open-source database vendor on root cause analysis and upstream contributions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Examples of the Difference You&#39;ll Make&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dig into the query and storage layers to explain latency differences between B-tree and LSM-based storage engines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze query plans and execution paths (planning, optimization, operators, and distributed execution) to find and fix sources of SQL latency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tune storage engine behavior (compaction, caching, and I/O) for Airbnb&#39;s workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement traffic prioritization at the storage layer for connection pooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive root cause analysis on high-severity incidents with our open-source vendor, and land fixes upstream.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of software engineering, including significant hands-on work on a database storage layer or query execution engine.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong SQL skills, plus an understanding of how queries are planned, optimized, and executed at the engine level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of storage engine internals (e.g., B-tree/LSM, compaction, indexing, I/O) and/or query processing (e.g., planning, optimization, execution operators).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with distributed databases (replication, consensus, transactions) is a strong plus, and familiarity with NewSQL systems like TiDB is a bonus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to own and dive deeply into a complex database codebase, ideally an open-source one. Upstream contributions are a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience analyzing and debugging high-severity production incidents, especially performance and latency problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Writes clean, testable, maintainable code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration and communication skills in a remote working environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ownership and a consistent track record of delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
